[2026-05-30 11:32:29] [INFO] [PreToolUse] Input: {"session_id":"b63b113f-845a-45c4-bb3d-eca702572f62","transcript_path":"C:\\Users\\Administrator\\.claude\\projects\\D--CodeDevelopment-CodeProject-claude-hk\\b63b113f-845a-45c4-bb3d-eca702572f62.jsonl","cwd":"D:\\CodeDevelopment\\CodeProject\\claude-hk","permission_mode":"plan","effort":{"level":"xhigh"},"hook_event_name":"PreToolUse","tool_name":"Agent","tool_input":{"description":"Design daily logger plan","prompt":"Design an implementation plan for adding a daily-rotating file logger to the claude_tap_plus Go project.\n\n## Requirements\n1. **Daily log files**: One log file per day, e.g., `.claude-tap-plus/.traces/2026-05-30.log`\n2. **Detailed debug logging**: Function enter/exit, parameter values, intermediate states, 10+ entries per module\n3. **Same directory as trace files**: The log files should go into the same base directory used by `internal/trace/` for JSONL trace output\n4. **Log format**: Include timestamp, level, module/function name, message\n\n## Current Codebase Context\n\n### Trace Output Directory\n- Default: `$HOME/.claude-tap-plus/.traces/` (via `trace.DefaultTraceDir()`)\n- Configurable via `--tap-output-dir` flag\n- The trace path is: `baseDir/{project}/{date}_{time}_{shortID}.jsonl`\n- Log files should go directly in `baseDir/` (e.g., `baseDir/2026-05-30.log`)\n\n### Current Logging\n- Uses standard Go `log` package with `log.SetFlags(log.Ltime | log.Lmicroseconds)` in main.go\n- Only ~15 `log.Printf`/`log.Fatalf` calls across entire codebase\n- No structured logging library\n\n### Project Structure\nKey files to add logging to:\n- `cmd/claude-tap/main.go` - CLI entry, proxy lifecycle, child process management, subcommand routing\n- `cmd/claude-tap/backend_cmd.go` - Backend subcommand entry\n- `internal/proxy/reverse.go` - Reverse proxy: request forwarding, header redaction, SSE/non-SSE, turn tracking\n- `internal/sse/reassembler.go` - SSE byte stream reassembler\n- `internal/sse/types.go` - SSE types\n- `internal/trace/writer.go` - JSONL trace writer with token stats\n- `internal/trace/anthropic.go` - Anthropic trace fields\n- `internal/usage/anthropic.go` - Anthropic token fields\n- `internal/usage/normalize.go` - Multi-provider normalization\n- `internal/backend/server.go` - HTTP server setup\n- `internal/backend/config.go` - Backend config\n- `internal/backend/api/router.go` - Route definitions\n- `internal/backend/api/issue_handler.go` - Issue API handlers\n- `internal/backend/api/session_handler.go` - Session API handlers\n- `internal/backend/api/health_handler.go` - Health check handler\n- `internal/backend/service/issue_service.go` - Issue business logic\n- `internal/backend/service/session_service.go` - Session business logic\n- `internal/backend/service/cleanup_service.go` - Cleanup service\n- `internal/backend/store/sqlite.go` - SQLite store with WAL mode\n- `internal/backend/store/migrations.go` - DB schema\n- `internal/backend/store/issue_store.go` - Issue store interface + impl\n- `internal/backend/store/store.go` - Store interfaces\n- `internal/backend/domain/` - Entity structs\n- `internal/session/` - Session push/pull/status\n- `internal/config/` - Client config, upstream URL detection\n\n### Design Constraints\n- Keep it simple — no external dependencies for logging, use stdlib\n- The logger should be a new internal package: `internal/logger/`\n- Init the logger early in main.go and backend_cmd.go\n- The logger should support both file output AND console output (dual-write like the shell skills do)\n- Date-based rotation: check date on each write, open new file if date changed\n- Thread-safe (the proxy handles concurrent requests)\n\n### Important: Trace directory for backend mode\nThe backend subcommand also needs logging. The backend uses a different config (`--db` flag for database path). For backend mode, logs should go next to the database file or in a default location.\n\nPlease produce a detailed plan covering:\n1. The logger package API and implementation\n2. How to initialize the logger in both proxy mode and backend mode\n3. Specific logging points for each key file (what to log at each point)\n4. How to handle the trace directory resolution for both modes\n","subagent_type":"Plan"},"tool_use_id":"call_e2f4fd8b056c48b7906e1bfe"}
