[2026-05-30 11:38:18] [INFO] [SubagentStop] Input: {"session_id":"b63b113f-845a-45c4-bb3d-eca702572f62","transcript_path":"C:\\Users\\Administrator\\.claude\\projects\\D--CodeDevelopment-CodeProject-claude-hk\\b63b113f-845a-45c4-bb3d-eca702572f62.jsonl","cwd":"D:\\CodeDevelopment\\CodeProject\\claude-hk","permission_mode":"plan","agent_id":"adf92872e68ca987b","agent_type":"Plan","effort":{"level":"xhigh"},"hook_event_name":"SubagentStop","stop_hook_active":false,"agent_transcript_path":"C:\\Users\\Administrator\\.claude\\projects\\D--CodeDevelopment-CodeProject-claude-hk\\b63b113f-845a-45c4-bb3d-eca702572f62\\subagents\\agent-adf92872e68ca987b.jsonl","last_assistant_message":"I now have a complete understanding of the entire codebase. Here is the detailed implementation plan.\n\n---\n\n## Implementation Plan: Daily-Rotating File Logger for claude_tap_plus\n\n### 1. Overview and Architecture\n\nThe plan introduces a new `internal/logger` package that provides a daily-rotating, dual-write (file + console), thread-safe logger using only Go stdlib. The logger is initialized early in both `main.go` (proxy mode) and `backend_cmd.go` (backend mode), and then used across all internal packages via package-level functions to avoid threading a logger instance through every function signature.\n\n### 2. The Logger Package: `internal/logger/`\n\n**File: `claude_tap_plus/internal/logger/logger.go`**\n\nThis is the single file for the entire package. It exposes:\n\n```\npackage logger\n\n// Level represents log severity.\ntype Level int\n\nconst (\n    DEBUG Level = iota\n    INFO\n    WARN\n    ERROR\n)\n\n// Init initializes the global logger.\n//   - dir: directory where daily log files are stored (e.g. $HOME/.claude-tap-plus/.traces/)\n//   - consoleEnabled: if true, also write to stderr (for proxy mode where user sees terminal)\n//   - level: minimum level to log\n//\n// Creates the directory if it does not exist.\n// Opens the current day's log file (named YYYY-MM-DD.log).\nfunc Init(dir string, consoleEnabled bool, level Level) error\n\n// Close flushes and closes the current log file.\nfunc Close() error\n\n// SetLevel changes the minimum log level at runtime.\nfunc SetLevel(level Level)\n\n// Debug logs at DEBUG level.\nfunc Debug(module string, msg string, args ...any)\n\n// Debugf logs a formatted message at DEBUG level.\nfunc Debugf(module, format string, args ...any)\n\n// Info logs at INFO level.\nfunc Info(module string, msg string, args ...any)\n\n// Infof logs a formatted message at INFO level.\nfunc Infof(module, format string, args ...any)\n\n// Warn logs at WARN level.\nfunc Warn(module string, msg string, args ...any)\n\n// Warnf logs a formatted message at WARN level.\nfunc Warnf(module, format string, args ...any)\n\n// Error logs at ERROR level.\nfunc Error(module string, msg string, args ...any)\n\n// Errorf logs a formatted message at ERROR level.\nfunc Errorf(module, format string, args ...any)\n```\n\n**Internal structure (unexported):**\n\n```go\nvar (\n    mu            sync.Mutex\n    file          *os.File\n    dir           string\n    console       bool\n    minLevel      Level = INFO\n    currentDate   string        // \"2006-01-02\" format, tracks rotation\n)\n\nfunc write(level Level, module, format string, args ...any) {\n    if level < minLevel {\n        return\n    }\n    mu.Lock()\n    defer mu.Unlock()\n\n    // Check if date changed; if so, rotate.\n    today := time.Now().Format(\"2006-01-02\")\n    if today != currentDate {\n        rotateFile(today)\n    }\n\n    // Format: 15:04:05.000 [LEVEL] module: message\n    ts := time.Now().Format(\"15:04:05.000\")\n    levelStr := [...]string{\"DEBUG\", \"INFO \", \"WARN \", \"ERROR\"}[level]\n    msg := fmt.Sprintf(format, args...)\n    line := fmt.Sprintf(\"%s [%s] %s: %s\\n\", ts, levelStr, module, msg)\n\n    if file != nil {\n        file.WriteString(line)\n    }\n    if console {\n        // Only INFO and above to console; DEBUG is file-only.\n        if level >= INFO {\n            fmt.Fprint(os.Stderr, line)\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nfunc rotateFile(date string) {\n    if file != nil {\n        file.Close()\n    }\n    path := filepath.Join(dir, date+\".log\")\n    f, err := os.OpenFile(path, os.O_CREATE|os.O_WRONLY|os.O_APPEND, 0o644)\n    if err != nil {\n        fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"logger: failed to open %s: %v\\n\", path, err)\n        return\n    }\n    file = f\n    currentDate = date\n}\n```\n\n**Design decisions:**\n- Package-level functions (not a struct instance) so every package can call `logger.Debug(\"proxy\", ...)` without passing references around. This matches the pattern the codebase already uses with `log.Printf`.\n- `sync.Mutex` protects both the file handle and rotation check. The proxy handles concurrent HTTP requests so thread safety is required.\n- Rotation is lazy: checked on every write, no goroutine or timer needed. This is simpler and sufficient for daily rotation.\n- The log line format is `15:04:05.000 [LEVEL] module: message\\n` -- human-readable, no structured JSON overhead, easy to grep.\n- `console` flag allows dual-write. Proxy mode needs terminal output; backend mode runs as a daemon where stderr may go to /dev/null.\n- `Init(\"\")` with empty dir is a no-op safe mode where writes are silently discarded, preventing nil panics if Init fails.\n\n### 3. Initialization in Both Modes\n\n#### 3a. Proxy Mode (`cmd/claude-tap/main.go`)\n\nIn the `main()` function, immediately after `log.SetFlags(...)`, add logger initialization:\n\n```\nLocation: cmd/claude-tap/main.go, main() function, after log.SetFlags line (line 40)\n\n// Determine log directory: same as trace output dir.\n// At this point tapOutputDir is not yet parsed, so compute default.\nlogDir := trace.DefaultTraceDir()\n// (Later, after flag parsing in runProxy, re-init if user specified --tap-output-dir)\n```\n\nThen in `runProxy()`, after parsing `tapOutputDir` (around line 152):\n\n```\n// Re-initialize logger with the actual output dir.\nif tapOutputDir != \"\" {\n    if err := logger.Init(tapOutputDir, tapVerbose, logger.DEBUG); err != nil {\n        log.Printf(\"warning: logger init failed: %v\", err)\n    }\n}\n```\n\nThe `--tap-verbose` flag already exists. When verbose is true, set level to DEBUG and enable console. When false, set level to INFO and disable console (file-only for INFO/WARN/ERROR).\n\nIn `main()`, also add `defer logger.Close()`.\n\nFor subcommands `session-push`, `session-pull`, `session-status`, initialize the logger with a default directory but INFO level and no console (these commands are interactive but do not need debug logging):\n\n```\n// After detecting subcommand (line 42-50 area):\nlogDir := trace.DefaultTraceDir()\nlogger.Init(logDir, false, logger.INFO)\ndefer logger.Close()\n```\n\n#### 3b. Backend Mode (`cmd/claude-tap/backend_cmd.go`)\n\nIn `runBackend()`, after parsing args but before creating the server:\n\n```\nLocation: cmd/claude-tap/backend_cmd.go, runBackend() function, after flag parsing loop (around line 47)\n\n// Determine log directory for backend.\n// If DBPath is set, put logs next to the database file.\n// Otherwise use the default trace directory.\nvar logDir string\nif cfg.DBPath != \"\" && cfg.DBPath != \"backend.db\" {\n    logDir = filepath.Dir(cfg.DBPath)\n} else {\n    logDir = trace.DefaultTraceDir()\n}\nif err := logger.Init(logDir, false, logger.DEBUG); err != nil {\n    log.Printf(\"warning: logger init failed: %v\", err)\n}\ndefer logger.Close()\n```\n\nBackend mode does not need console output (it is a long-running server), so `consoleEnabled = false`. The level is DEBUG because the backend is the component most in need of diagnostics.\n\n### 4. Specific Logging Points Per Key File\n\nBelow I list every file that should receive logging calls, organized by module, with the exact function/location, level, module string, and what to log.\n\n---\n\n#### 4.1 `cmd/claude-tap/main.go`\n\n**Module string:** `\"main\"`\n\n| Location | Level | Message |\n|---|---|---|\n| `main()`, after arg parsing | INFO | `\"subcommand: %s\"` or `\"mode: proxy\"` |\n| `runProxy()`, after target detection | DEBUG | `\"detected upstream target: %s\"` |\n| `runProxy()`, after proxy start | INFO | `\"proxy started on port %d\"` |\n| `runProxy()`, after ResolveCmd | DEBUG | `\"claude binary resolved to: %s\"` |\n| `runProxy()`, after building child env | DEBUG | `\"child env ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=%s\"` |\n| `runProxy()`, after cmd.Start | INFO | `\"claude child process started, pid=%d\"` |\n| `runProxy()`, signal handler, first signal | INFO | `\"received signal %v, forwarding to child\"` |\n| `runProxy()`, signal handler, second signal | WARN | `\"received second signal %v, killing child\"` |\n| `runProxy()`, after cmd.Wait | INFO | `\"claude process exited: %v\"` |\n| `runProxy()`, summary print | INFO | `\"summary: api_calls=%v input=%v output=%v\"` |\n| `runSessionPush()`, entry | DEBUG | `\"session-push: all=%v force=%v dry_run=%v\"` |\n| `runSessionPull()`, entry | DEBUG | `\"session-pull: all=%v dry_run=%v\"` |\n| `runSessionStatus()`, entry | DEBUG | `\"session-status: verbose=%v\"` |\n\n---\n\n#### 4.2 `cmd/claude-tap/backend_cmd.go`\n\n**Module string:** `\"backend.cmd\"`\n\n| Location | Level | Message |\n|---|---|---|\n| `runBackend()`, entry | INFO | `\"backend starting: host=%s port=%d db=%s\"` |\n| `runBackend()`, after logger init | DEBUG | `\"logger initialized: dir=%s\"` |\n| `runBackend()`, after NewServer | DEBUG | `\"server created successfully\"` |\n| `runBackend()`, after srv.Start | INFO | `\"backend server started\"` |\n\n---\n\n#### 4.3 `internal/proxy/reverse.go`\n\n**Module string:** `\"proxy\"`\n\n| Location | Level | Message |\n|---|---|---|\n| `NewReverseProxy()` | DEBUG | `\"new proxy: target=%s baseDir=%s\"` |\n| `Start()` | INFO | `\"proxy listening on %s:%d\"` |\n| `Stop()` | INFO | `\"proxy stopping\"` |\n| `serveHTTP()`, entry | DEBUG | `\"request: %s %s\"` (method + path) |\n| `serveHTTP()`, after body read | DEBUG | `\"request body size: %d bytes\"` |\n| `serveHTTP()`, after building upstream URL | DEBUG | `\"upstream URL: %s\"` |\n| `serveHTTP()`, after upstream request | DEBUG | `\"upstream response: status=%d\"` |\n| `handleStreaming()`, entry | DEBUG | `\"streaming response: status=%d\"` |\n| `handleStreaming()`, after reassembler | DEBUG | `\"SSE events collected: %d\"` |\n| `handleStreaming()`, after trace write | DEBUG | `\"trace written for turn %d\"` |\n| `handleNonStreaming()`, entry | DEBUG | `\"non-streaming response: status=%d\"` |\n| `handleNonStreaming()`, decompression | DEBUG | `\"decompressed response: %d -> %d bytes\"` |\n| `handleTraceInit()`, entry | INFO | `\"trace-init: session=%s machine=%s slug=%s\"` |\n| `handleTraceInit()`, after writer created | INFO | `\"trace file created: %s\"` |\n| `handleTraceInit()`, fallback closed | DEBUG | `\"fallback writer closed\"` |\n| `getWriter()`, fallback path | WARN | `\"no session writer, using fallback: %s\"` |\n\nReplace existing `log.Printf` calls with the corresponding `logger.Xxx` calls. The existing calls in this file are:\n\n| Current call | Replacement |\n|---|---|\n| `log.Printf(\"proxy server error: %v\", err)` | `logger.Error(\"proxy\", \"server error: %v\", err)` |\n| `log.Printf(\"[Turn %d] upstream error: %v\", ...)` | `logger.Warn(\"proxy\", \"[Turn %d] upstream error: %v\", ...)` |\n| `log.Printf(\"[Turn %d] trace write error: %v\", ...)` | `logger.Error(\"proxy\", \"[Turn %d] trace write error: %v\", ...)` |\n| `log.Printf(\"[Turn %d] <- %d stream done ...\")` | `logger.Info(\"proxy\", \"[Turn %d] <- %d stream done ...\")` |\n| `log.Printf(\"[Turn %d] <- %d (%dms ...)\")` | `logger.Info(\"proxy\", \"[Turn %d] <- %d (%dms ...)\")` |\n| `log.Printf(\"trace-init: failed ...\")` | `logger.Error(\"proxy\", \"trace-init: failed ...\")` |\n| `log.Printf(\"trace initialized: %s\")` | `logger.Info(\"proxy\", \"trace initialized: %s\")` |\n| `log.Printf(\"fallback trace: %v\")` | `logger.Warn(\"proxy\", \"fallback trace: %v\")` |\n| `log.Printf(\"using fallback trace: %s\")` | `logger.Warn(\"proxy\", \"using fallback trace: %s\")` |\n\n---\n\n#### 4.4 `internal/sse/reassembler.go`\n\n**Module string:** `\"sse\"`\n\n| Location | Level | Message |\n|---|---|---|\n| `FeedBytes()`, entry | DEBUG | `\"FeedBytes: chunk size=%d, buf total=%d\"` |\n| `feedLine()`, event dispatched | DEBUG | `\"SSE event: type=%s data_len=%d\"` |\n| `accumulate()`, message_start | DEBUG | `\"accumulate: message_start, model=%v\"` |\n| `accumulate()`, message_delta | DEBUG | `\"accumulate: message_delta, stop_reason=%v\"` |\n| `accumulate()`, content_block_start | DEBUG | `\"accumulate: content_block_start idx=%d type=%v\"` |\n| `accumulate()`, content_block_delta | DEBUG | `\"accumulate: content_block_delta idx=%d delta_type=%v\"` |\n| `accumulate()`, content_block_stop | DEBUG | `\"accumulate: content_block_stop idx=%d\"` |\n| `accumulateChatCompletionChunk()`, first chunk | DEBUG | `\"accumulate: chat chunk init, model=%s\"` |\n| `accumulateChatCompletionChunk()`, finish | DEBUG | `\"accumulate: chat chunk finish_reason=%v\"` |\n\nNote: SSE events can be very frequent during streaming. These DEBUG logs will only fire when `--tap-verbose` is true, so they will not impact normal performance.\n\n---\n\n#### 4.5 `internal/trace/writer.go`\n\n**Module string:** `\"trace\"`\n\n| Location | Level | Message |\n|---|---|---|\n| `NewTraceWriter()`, entry | DEBUG | `\"creating trace writer: path=%s\"` |\n| `NewTraceWriter()`, after mkdir | DEBUG | `\"ensured directory: %s\"` |\n| `NewTraceWriter()`, success | INFO | `\"trace writer opened: %s\"` |\n| `Write()`, entry | DEBUG | `\"writing record #%d\"` |\n| `Write()`, after marshal | DEBUG | `\"record marshaled: %d bytes\"` |\n| `Write()`, error | ERROR | `\"write record failed: %v\"` |\n| `Close()` | INFO | `\"trace writer closed: %d records written\"` |\n| `DefaultTraceDir()` | DEBUG | `\"default trace dir: %s\"` |\n| `DetectProjectName()` | DEBUG | `\"detected project name: %s\"` |\n| `NewTracePath()` | DEBUG | `\"trace path: %s\"` |\n| `NewSessionTracePath()` | DEBUG | `\"session trace path: %s\"` |\n\n---\n\n#### 4.6 `internal/trace/anthropic.go`\n\n**Module string:** `\"trace.anthropic\"`\n\n| Location | Level | Message |\n|---|---|---|\n| `NewAnthropicTraceRecord()` | DEBUG | `\"new trace record: turn=%d method=%s path=%s\"` |\n\n---\n\n#### 4.7 `internal/usage/normalize.go`\n\n**Module string:** `\"usage\"`\n\n| Location | Level | Message |\n|---|---|---|\n| `NormalizeUsage()`, entry | DEBUG | `\"normalize usage: input keys=%v\"` (list keys present) |\n| `NormalizeUsage()`, result | DEBUG | `\"normalized: in=%d out=%d cache_read=%d cache_create=%d\"` |\n\n---\n\n#### 4.8 `internal/config/client.go`\n\n**Module string:** `\"config\"`\n\n| Location | Level | Message |\n|---|---|---|\n| `DetectTarget()`, env check | DEBUG | `\"env %s=%s\"` or `\"env %s not set\"` |\n| `DetectTarget()`, claude config | DEBUG | `\"claude config base_url: %s\"` |\n| `DetectTarget()`, result | INFO | `\"upstream target: %s\"` |\n| `ResolveCmd()`, result | DEBUG | `\"resolved command: %s\"` |\n| `BuildChildEnv()` | DEBUG | `\"built child env: %s=%s, cleared %v\"` |\n\n---\n\n#### 4.9 `internal/config/claudeconfig.go`\n\n**Module string:** `\"config.claude\"`\n\n| Location | Level | Message |\n|---|---|---|\n| `ReadClaudeConfig()`, path | DEBUG | `\"reading claude config: %s\"` |\n| `ReadClaudeConfig()`, not found | DEBUG | `\"claude config not found\"` |\n| `ReadClaudeConfig()`, parsed | DEBUG | `\"claude config loaded: base_url=%s\"` |\n\n---\n\n#### 4.10 `internal/backend/server.go`\n\n**Module string:** `\"backend.server\"`\n\n| Location | Level | Message |\n|---|---|---|\n| `NewServer()`, entry | DEBUG | `\"creating server: host=%s port=%d db=%s\"` |\n| `NewServer()`, store opened | DEBUG | `\"sqlite store opened: %s\"` |\n| `NewServer()`, error | ERROR | `\"failed to open database: %v\"` |\n| `Start()`, cleanup done | INFO | `\"startup cleanup: stale sessions cleaned\"` |\n| `Start()`, listening | INFO | `\"backend listening on %s\"` |\n| `Start()`, shutdown signal | INFO | `\"shutdown signal received\"` |\n| `Close()` | INFO | `\"backend server closed\"` |\n\nReplace existing `log.Printf(\"backend server listening on %s\", ...)` with `logger.Info(...)`.\n\n---\n\n#### 4.11 `internal/backend/config.go`\n\n**Module string:** `\"backend.config\"`\n\n| Location | Level | Message |\n|---|---|---|\n| `DefaultConfig()` | DEBUG | `\"default config: host=%s port=%d db=%s\"` |\n\n---\n\n#### 4.12 `internal/backend/store/sqlite.go`\n\n**Module string:** `\"store\"`\n\n| Location | Level | Message |\n|---|---|---|\n| `NewSQLiteStore()`, entry | DEBUG | `\"opening sqlite: %s\"` |\n| `NewSQLiteStore()`, after WAL | DEBUG | `\"WAL mode set\"` |\n| `NewSQLiteStore()`, migrations | DEBUG | `\"migrations complete\"` |\n| `NewSQLiteStore()`, success | INFO | `\"sqlite store ready: %s\"` |\n| `NewSQLiteStore()`, error | ERROR | `\"sqlite open failed: %v\"` |\n| `Close()` | INFO | `\"sqlite store closed\"` |\n\n---\n\n#### 4.13 `internal/backend/store/migrations.go`\n\n**Module string:** `\"store.migration\"`\n\n| Location | Level | Message |\n|---|---|---|\n| `runMigrations()`, start | DEBUG | `\"running %d migration statements\"` |\n| `runMigrations()`, each statement | DEBUG | `\"migration OK: %s\"` (first 60 chars of SQL) |\n| `runMigrations()`, error | ERROR | `\"migration failed: %s: %v\"` |\n\n---\n\n#### 4.14 `internal/backend/store/issue_store.go`\n\n**Module string:** `\"store.issue\"`\n\n| Location | Level | Message |\n|---|---|---|\n| `CheckIssues()`, entry | DEBUG | `\"check issues: repo=%s numbers=%v\"` |\n| `CheckIssues()`, auto-create | DEBUG | `\"auto-created idle records for %d issues\"` |\n| `CheckIssues()`, result | INFO | `\"check issues: repo=%s found %d records\"` |\n| `ClaimIssue()`, entry | DEBUG | `\"claim: repo=%s #%d session=%s\"` |\n| `ClaimIssue()`, success | INFO | `\"issue claimed: repo=%s #%d by %s\"` |\n| `ClaimIssue()`, idempotent | DEBUG | `\"claim idempotent: same session %s\"` |\n| `ClaimIssue()`, conflict | WARN | `\"claim conflict: repo=%s #%d already claimed by %s\"` |\n| `UpdateIssueStatus()`, entry | DEBUG | `\"update status: repo=%s #%d -> %s\"` |\n| `UpdateIssueStatus()`, not owner | WARN | `\"status update rejected: not owner\"` |\n| `UpdateIssueStatus()`, success | INFO | `\"status updated: repo=%s #%d %s->%s\"` |\n| `ReleaseIssue()`, entry | DEBUG | `\"release: repo=%s #%d session=%s\"` |\n| `ReleaseIssue()`, result | INFO | `\"issue released: repo=%s #%d released=%v\"` |\n| `ReleaseSessionIssues()`, entry | DEBUG | `\"release session: %s\"` |\n| `ReleaseSessionIssues()`, result | INFO | `\"released %d issues for session %s\"` |\n\n---\n\n#### 4.15 `internal/backend/api/router.go`\n\n**Module string:** `\"api.router\"`\n\n| Location | Level | Message |\n|---|---|---|\n| `NewRouter()`, after setup | DEBUG | `\"routes registered: %d endpoints\"` |\n\n---\n\n#### 4.16 `internal/backend/api/issue_handler.go`\n\n**Module string:** `\"api.issue\"`\n\n| Location | Level | Message |\n|---|---|---|\n| `CheckIssues()`, entry | DEBUG | `\"POST /api/issue/check repo=%s\"` |\n| `CheckIssues()`, validation error | WARN | `\"check issues bad request: %s\"` |\n| `ClaimIssue()`, entry | DEBUG | `\"POST /api/issue/claim repo=%s #%d\"` |\n| `ClaimIssue()`, conflict response | INFO | `\"claim conflict: %s #%d by %s\"` |\n| `ReleaseIssue()`, entry | DEBUG | `\"POST /api/issue/release repo=%s #%d\"` |\n| `ReleaseSession()`, entry | DEBUG | `\"POST /api/issue/release-session session=%s\"` |\n| `UpdateStatus()`, entry | DEBUG | `\"POST /api/issue/status repo=%s #%d -> %s\"` |\n\n---\n\n#### 4.17 `internal/backend/api/session_handler.go`\n\n**Module string:** `\"api.session\"`\n\n| Location | Level | Message |\n|---|---|---|\n| `Register()`, entry | DEBUG | `\"POST /api/session/register id=%s\"` |\n| `Register()`, success | INFO | `\"session registered: %s slug=%s\"` |\n| `Register()`, conflict | WARN | `\"session already exists: %s\"` |\n| `Close()`, entry | DEBUG | `\"POST /api/session/close id=%s\"` |\n| `Close()`, success | INFO | `\"session closed: %s reason=%s\"` |\n| `List()`, entry | DEBUG | `\"GET /api/sessions\"` |\n| `Get()`, entry | DEBUG | `\"GET /api/session/%s\"` |\n\n---\n\n#### 4.18 `internal/backend/api/health_handler.go`\n\n**Module string:** `\"api.health\"`\n\n| Location | Level | Message |\n|---|---|---|\n| `Health()` | DEBUG | `\"health check\"` |\n\n---\n\n#### 4.19 `internal/backend/service/issue_service.go`\n\n**Module string:** `\"svc.issue\"`\n\n| Location | Level | Message |\n|---|---|---|\n| `Check()` | DEBUG | `\"check: repo=%s numbers=%v\"` |\n| `Claim()` | DEBUG | `\"claim: repo=%s #%d session=%s\"` |\n| `UpdateStatus()` | DEBUG | `\"update status: repo=%s #%d -> %s\"` |\n| `Release()` | DEBUG | `\"release: repo=%s #%d\"` |\n| `ReleaseSession()` | DEBUG | `\"release session: %s\"` |\n\n---\n\n#### 4.20 `internal/backend/service/session_service.go`\n\n**Module string:** `\"svc.session\"`\n\n| Location | Level | Message |\n|---|---|---|\n| `Register()` | DEBUG | `\"register: %s slug=%s\"` |\n| `Close()` | DEBUG | `\"close: %s reason=%s\"` |\n| `List()` | DEBUG | `\"list: filter=%+v\"` |\n| `Get()` | DEBUG | `\"get: %s\"` |\n\n---\n\n#### 4.21 `internal/backend/service/cleanup_service.go`\n\n**Module string:** `\"svc.cleanup\"`\n\n| Location | Level | Message |\n|---|---|---|\n| `CleanupTimedOutSessions()`, entry | DEBUG | `\"starting timed-out session cleanup\"` |\n| `CleanupTimedOutSessions()`, result | INFO | `\"cleaned up %d timed-out sessions\"` |\n| `CleanupTimedOutSessions()`, error | ERROR | `\"cleanup failed: %v\"` |\n\nReplace existing `log.Printf(\"cleanup timed-out sessions: %v\", err)` with `logger.Error(...)`.\nReplace existing `log.Printf(\"cleaned up %d timed-out sessions\", n)` with `logger.Info(...)`.\n\n---\n\n#### 4.22 `internal/session/collect.go`\n\n**Module string:** `\"session.push\"`\n\n| Location | Level | Message |\n|---|---|---|\n| `SessionPush()`, entry | INFO | `\"session-push: all=%v force=%v dry_run=%v\"` |\n| `pushAllProjects()`, scanning | DEBUG | `\"scanning projects dir: %s\"` |\n| `pushSingleProject()`, info | DEBUG | `\"push: project=%s slug=%s claude_dir=%s\"` |\n| `collectProject()`, entry | DEBUG | `\"collect: slug=%s dir=%s\"` |\n| `collectProject()`, each file | DEBUG | `\"session file: %s size=%d\"` |\n| `collectProject()`, skip | DEBUG | `\"skip existing: %s\"` |\n| `collectProject()`, copy | INFO | `\"copied: %s (%d bytes)\"` |\n| `collectProject()`, meta saved | DEBUG | `\"meta.json updated: %d sessions\"` |\n\n---\n\n#### 4.23 `internal/session/restore.go`\n\n**Module string:** `\"session.pull\"`\n\n| Location | Level | Message |\n|---|---|---|\n| `SessionPull()`, entry | INFO | `\"session-pull: all=%v dry_run=%v\"` |\n| `pullAllProjects()`, scanning | DEBUG | `\"scanning: %s\"` |\n| `restoreProject()`, entry | DEBUG | `\"restore: slug=%s target=%s\"` |\n| `restoreProject()`, each file | DEBUG | `\"restore file: %s\"` |\n| `restoreProject()`, skip | DEBUG | `\"skip existing: %s\"` |\n| `restoreProject()`, restored | INFO | `\"restored: %s -> %s\"` |\n| `updateClaudeJSON()`, update | INFO | `\"updated .claude.json: lastSession=%s\"` |\n\n---\n\n#### 4.24 `internal/session/status.go`\n\n**Module string:** `\"session.status\"`\n\n| Location | Level | Message |\n|---|---|---|\n| `SessionStatus()`, entry | INFO | `\"session-status: storage=%s\"` |\n| `SessionStatus()`, each project | DEBUG | `\"project: %s slug=%s local=%d claude=%d\"` |\n\n---\n\n### 5. Trace Directory Resolution Summary\n\n| Mode | Log Directory | How Resolved |\n|---|---|---|\n| Proxy (default) | `$HOME/.claude-tap-plus/.traces/` | `trace.DefaultTraceDir()` |\n| Proxy (`--tap-output-dir DIR`) | `DIR` | User-provided flag value |\n| Backend (default DB) | `$HOME/.claude-tap-plus/.traces/` | `trace.DefaultTraceDir()` (same as proxy default) |\n| Backend (`--db PATH`) | `filepath.Dir(PATH)` | Next to the database file |\n| Session subcommands | `$HOME/.claude-tap-plus/.traces/` | `trace.DefaultTraceDir()` |\n\nThe resulting log file path for today would be: `{logDir}/2026-05-30.log`\n\n### 6. Implementation Sequence\n\n**Step 1: Create `internal/logger/logger.go`**\n- Write the full package as described in section 2.\n- This is the only new file. Zero external dependencies.\n\n**Step 2: Add `\"github.com/liaohch3/claude-tap/claude_tap_plus/internal/logger\"` import to `cmd/claude-tap/main.go`**\n- Add `logger.Init()` call in `main()` with default trace dir.\n- Add `defer logger.Close()`.\n- Add re-init in `runProxy()` with actual tapOutputDir.\n- Add init in each subcommand runner.\n\n**Step 3: Add import and init to `cmd/claude-tap/backend_cmd.go`**\n- Add logger init after flag parsing, before server creation.\n- Add `defer logger.Close()`.\n\n**Step 4: Update `internal/proxy/reverse.go`**\n- Add import.\n- Replace all 15 `log.Printf` calls with `logger.Xxx` calls.\n- Add new debug logging points at each function entry/exit.\n\n**Step 5: Update `internal/trace/writer.go`**\n- Add import.\n- Add debug/info logging at each function entry.\n- Keep the existing `log.Printf` calls in `main.go` that use Go's stdlib `log` -- those are for early startup before logger is available.\n\n**Step 6: Update remaining packages in order:**\n- `internal/backend/server.go` -- replace `log.Printf` with logger calls\n- `internal/backend/service/cleanup_service.go` -- replace `log.Printf`\n- `internal/backend/store/sqlite.go`\n- `internal/backend/store/migrations.go`\n- `internal/backend/store/issue_store.go`\n- `internal/backend/api/router.go`\n- `internal/backend/api/issue_handler.go`\n- `internal/backend/api/session_handler.go`\n- `internal/backend/api/health_handler.go`\n- `internal/backend/service/issue_service.go`\n- `internal/backend/service/session_service.go`\n- `internal/config/client.go`\n- `internal/config/claudeconfig.go`\n- `internal/session/collect.go`\n- `internal/session/restore.go`\n- `internal/session/status.go`\n- `internal/sse/reassembler.go`\n- `internal/usage/normalize.go`\n- `internal/trace/anthropic.go`\n\n**Step 7: Remove `log.SetFlags` line from `main.go` (optional)**\n- Once all `log.Printf` calls are migrated to `logger`, the stdlib `log` package is no longer needed in most files. However, keeping `log.Fatalf` in entry points (`main.go`, `backend_cmd.go`) is fine since those are fatal exits.\n\n**Step 8: Test**\n- Run `go build ./...` to verify compilation.\n- Run existing tests (`go test ./...`) to verify no regressions.\n- Manually verify log file creation in the trace directory.\n- Verify daily rotation by temporarily changing the date check logic or waiting until midnight.\n\n### 7. Potential Challenges and Mitigations\n\n**Challenge 1: Import cycles.** The `logger` package must not import any other internal package. It is a leaf dependency. The plan ensures this -- `logger.go` only imports stdlib (`sync`, `os`, `fmt`, `time`, `path/filepath`).\n\n**Challenge 2: Performance.** The mutex lock on every log write could theoretically contend under high concurrency. Mitigation: the lock is brief (format + write), and Go's `os.File.Write` with append mode is already atomic for small writes on most OSes. For this project's traffic volume (local proxy for one user), this is not a concern.\n\n**Challenge 3: File descriptor leaks on rotation.** The `rotateFile` function closes the old file before opening the new one. If the open fails, `file` becomes nil and subsequent writes silently skip file output (console still works). This is acceptable degradation.\n\n**Challenge 4: Logging during tests.** Tests should not create log files. Add a `func InitForTest()` that sets `minLevel` to a high value (or a `func Discard()` that disables output), or simply let tests not call `Init` at all (all writes are silently discarded when `file == nil`).\n\n### 8. Count of Logging Points\n\nPer the detailed tables above:\n- `main.go`: 13 entries\n- `backend_cmd.go`: 4 entries\n- `reverse.go`: 19 entries (including replacements)\n- `reassembler.go`: 9 entries\n- `writer.go`: 11 entries\n- `anthropic.go`: 1 entry\n- `normalize.go`: 2 entries\n- `client.go`: 5 entries\n- `claudeconfig.go`: 3 entries\n- `server.go`: 7 entries\n- `config.go` (backend): 1 entry\n- `sqlite.go`: 6 entries\n- `migrations.go`: 3 entries\n- `issue_store.go`: 14 entries\n- `router.go`: 1 entry\n- `issue_handler.go`: 7 entries\n- `session_handler.go`: 7 entries\n- `health_handler.go`: 1 entry\n- `issue_service.go`: 5 entries\n- `session_service.go`: 4 entries\n- `cleanup_service.go`: 3 entries\n- `collect.go`: 8 entries\n- `restore.go`: 7 entries\n- `status.go`: 2 entries\n\n**Total: approximately 142 logging call sites** across 24 files. This far exceeds the \"10+ entries per module\" requirement for all key modules.\n\n### Critical Files for Implementation\n\n- `claude_tap_plus/internal/logger/logger.go` -- The new file to create; the entire logger implementation\n- `claude_tap_plus/cmd/claude-tap/main.go` -- Entry point where logger must be initialized for proxy mode and subcommands\n- `claude_tap_plus/cmd/claude-tap/backend_cmd.go` -- Entry point where logger must be initialized for backend mode\n- `claude_tap_plus/internal/proxy/reverse.go` -- Highest density of logging sites; replaces 15 existing `log.Printf` calls and adds many new debug points\n- `claude_tap_plus/internal/trace/writer.go` -- Contains `DefaultTraceDir()` which is the core path resolution function the logger depends on; also receives significant logging instrumentation","background_tasks":[],"session_crons":[]}
