[2026-05-30 15:42:30] [INFO] [PostToolUse] Input: {"session_id":"b63b113f-845a-45c4-bb3d-eca702572f62","transcript_path":"C:\\Users\\Administrator\\.claude\\projects\\D--CodeDevelopment-CodeProject-claude-hk\\b63b113f-845a-45c4-bb3d-eca702572f62.jsonl","cwd":"D:\\CodeDevelopment\\CodeProject\\claude-hk\\claude_tap_plus","permission_mode":"default","agent_id":"af2c7f9be3c13caee","agent_type":"Explore","hook_event_name":"PostToolUse","tool_name":"WebSearch","tool_input":{"query":"Claude Code CLI clear command behavior session management"},"tool_response":{"query":"Claude Code CLI clear command behavior session management","results":["I'll perform a web search to find information about Claude Code CLI clear command behavior and session management.\n**🌐 Z.ai Built-in Tool: web_search_prime**\n\n**Input:**\n```json\n{\"search_query\":\"Claude Code CLI clear command behavior session management\"}\n```\n\n*Executing on server...*","**Output:**\n**web_search_prime_result_summary:** [{\"text\": [{\"title\": \"Add session cleanup/delete commands #35036 - GitHub\", \"link\": \"https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/issues/35036\", \"content\": \"Sessions accumulate over time with no way to clean them up from the CLI. The only options are: Manually deleting .jsonl files from ~/.claude/ ...\"...\n                                                \n**🌐 Z.ai Built-in Tool: web_search_prime**\n\n**Input:**\n```json\n{\"search_query\":\"\\\"Claude Code\\\" \\\"/clear\\\" command session behavior\"}\n```\n\n*Executing on server...*","**Output:**\n**web_search_prime_result_summary:** [{\"text\": [{\"title\": \"Commands - Claude Code Docs\", \"link\": \"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/commands\", \"content\": \"Between sessions. /clear starts fresh on a new task while keeping project memory. /resume and /branch let you return to or fork an earlier conversation. / ...\", \"refer\": \"ref_1\"}, {\"ti...\n                                                \nBased on my web search, here's a comprehensive overview of Claude Code CLI clear command behavior and session management:\n\n## /clear Command Behavior\n\n### What /clear Does:\n- **Clears conversation history** from Claude's context window\n- **Frees up context** by removing previous messages\n- **Starts fresh** for new tasks\n- **Can also be invoked as /reset or /new**\n\n### Session Management:\n- **Creates a new session** instead of clearing in-place (according to GitHub issues)\n- **Maintains project memory** while providing a fresh start\n- **Wipes the current conversation entirely** from the active session\n- **Keeps session files** for potential resuming later\n\n### Key Behaviors:\n1. **Context Reset**: Removes all conversation history and frees context\n2. **Performance Improvement**: Helps with long sessions that may have accumulated irrelevant context\n3. **Task Boundaries**: Best used to reset between unrelated tasks\n4. **Session Persistence**: Unlike manual deletion, /clear doesn't delete the session file - it just clears the conversation within it\n\n### Related Session Commands:\n- **/resume**: Return to or fork an earlier conversation\n- **/branch**: Create a fork from an earlier conversation point\n- **/list**: List available sessions\n- **Manual deletion**: Navigate to ~/.claude/ to delete .jsonl files\n\n### Issues and Considerations:\n- Some users report that /clear creates a new session with a multi-second delay\n- There are feature requests for better visual feedback when clearing\n- Users sometimes prefer starting a new session instead of using /clear for \"cleaner\" behavior\n- Session files accumulate over time, requiring manual cleanup\n\n### Best Practices:\n- Use /clear when you need to reset context between unrelated tasks\n- If you've corrected Claude more than twice on similar issues, consider clearing\n- Manual session deletion may be needed for old, test, or sensitive sessions\n- The command helps maintain performance by preventing overly long conversation histories\n\nThis gives you a clear picture of how the /clear command works within Claude Code's session management system and the various options available for managing your conversations and sessions."],"durationSeconds":18.682145199999212,"searchCount":2},"tool_use_id":"call_cf3a95f4bda945fe9bb6d8eb","duration_ms":18682}
