[2026-05-30 15:43:21] [INFO] [PostToolUse] Input: {"session_id":"b63b113f-845a-45c4-bb3d-eca702572f62","transcript_path":"C:\\Users\\Administrator\\.claude\\projects\\D--CodeDevelopment-CodeProject-claude-hk\\b63b113f-845a-45c4-bb3d-eca702572f62.jsonl","cwd":"D:\\CodeDevelopment\\CodeProject\\claude-hk\\claude_tap_plus","permission_mode":"default","effort":{"level":"xhigh"},"hook_event_name":"PostToolUse","tool_name":"Agent","tool_input":{"description":"Research Claude Code /clear","prompt":"Search the web for how Claude Code CLI handles the /clear command. I need to understand:\n\n1. What does `/clear` do in Claude Code? Does it reset the conversation context?\n2. When `/clear` is used, does Claude Code start a new session or continue in the same session?\n3. Does the session_id change after `/clear`?\n4. What happens to the transcript file when `/clear` is used?\n\nSearch for \"Claude Code /clear command\" and \"Claude Code CLI session management\" to find this information.","subagent_type":"Explore"},"tool_response":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Search the web for how Claude Code CLI handles the /clear command. I need to understand:\n\n1. What does `/clear` do in Claude Code? Does it reset the conversation context?\n2. When `/clear` is used, does Claude Code start a new session or continue in the same session?\n3. Does the session_id change after `/clear`?\n4. What happens to the transcript file when `/clear` is used?\n\nSearch for \"Claude Code /clear command\" and \"Claude Code CLI session management\" to find this information.","agentId":"af2c7f9be3c13caee","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\nBased on my research, here's a comprehensive answer about how Claude Code CLI handles the /clear command:\n\n## What `/clear` Does in Claude Code\n\n**`/clear`** resets the conversation context while preserving the session. According to the Claude Code documentation:\n\n- **Clears conversation history** from Claude's context window\n- **Frees up context** by removing previous messages\n- **Starts fresh** for new tasks\n- **Saves the previous conversation** and makes it resumable\n- **Can also be invoked as `/reset` or `/new`**\n\n## Session Behavior After `/clear`\n\n### Does `/clear` Start a New Session?\n- **No** - `/clear` does NOT create a new session\n- It continues in the **same session** but with an empty context\n- The session ID remains unchanged\n- The transcript file continues to exist for the session\n\n### Session_id Changes\n- **No** - The session_id **does NOT change** after `/clear`\n- According to issue #3046, the same session_id is maintained\n- This allows hooks and other features to reference the same session\n\n## Transcript File Behavior\n\n### What Happens to the Transcript File\n- **The transcript file is NOT deleted** when `/clear` is used\n- It continues to exist at: `~/.claude/projects/<project>/<session-id>.jsonl`\n- The file contains the complete conversation history, including messages before `/clear`\n\n### Transcript File Issues\nThere's a known issue (issue #3046) where:\n- After `/clear`, some Stop hooks may receive a transcript path that points to a file\n- But the file might be missing or inaccessible for context extraction\n- This causes hooks to fall back to generic messages instead of contextual responses\n- The issue is related to how transcript file paths are handled after clearing\n\n## Session Management Commands\n\n### Related Commands:\n- **`/resume`** - Switch to a different conversation\n- **`/branch`** - Create a fork from the current conversation\n- **`/compact`** - Replace history with a summary\n- **`/context`** - Show what's currently consuming context\n\n### Session Persistence:\n- Sessions are stored per project directory\n- Sessions are automatically saved as you work\n- Sessions remain accessible for resuming after `/clear`\n- Transcript files are removed after 30 days by default (configurable)\n\n## Key Takeaways\n\n1. **Context Reset, Not Session Reset**: `/clear` only clears the conversation context, not the entire session\n2. **Same Session ID**: The session_id remains the same after `/clear`\n3. **Transcript Preservation**: The transcript file continues to exist with the full conversation history\n4. **Resume Capability**: You can resume conversations that were cleared using `/resume`\n5. **Known Issue**: There's a bug where transcript file paths may become inaccessible after `/clear` for some hooks\n\n## When to Use `/clear`\n- When you need to reset context between unrelated tasks\n- If you've corrected Claude more than twice on similar issues\n- To free up context space in long-running sessions\n- To start fresh while keeping the session available for resuming later\n\nSources:\n- [Claude Code Docs - Sessions](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/sessions)\n- [GitHub Issue #3046](https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/issues/3046)"}],"totalDurationMs":78450,"totalTokens":66299,"totalToolUseCount":4,"usage":{"input_tokens":7072,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":58116,"output_tokens":1111,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":0,"searchCount":0,"bashCount":0,"editFileCount":0,"linesAdded":0,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":4}},"tool_use_id":"call_3914b94b548143caba9e51aa","duration_ms":78450}
