[2026-05-30 16:52:13] [DEBUG] [PostToolBatch] os=windows python=/d/CodeDevelopment/CodeProject/claude-hk/.claude/localLanguage/python/python.exe
[2026-05-30 16:52:13] [INFO] [PostToolBatch] Input: {"session_id":"85b4b220-e119-417e-b974-e5edde848812","transcript_path":"C:\\Users\\Administrator\\.claude\\projects\\D--CodeDevelopment-CodeProject-claude-hk\\85b4b220-e119-417e-b974-e5edde848812.jsonl","cwd":"D:\\CodeDevelopment\\CodeProject\\claude-hk","permission_mode":"plan","effort":{"level":"xhigh"},"hook_event_name":"PostToolBatch","tool_calls":[{"tool_name":"Agent","tool_input":{"description":"Design implementation plan","prompt":"Design an implementation plan for the three CLI enhancements described in `doc/otherDoc/2026-05-30/claude-tap-plus-cli-enhancements.md`. Here is the full context:\n\n## Current Codebase\n\n### main.go (`cmd/claude-tap/main.go`)\n- Entry point, parses subcommands (session-push/pull/status, backend, help)\n- Default: `runProxy(args)` for proxy mode\n- Already parses: `--tap-target`, `--tap-port`, `--tap-output-dir`, `--tap-verbose`\n- Missing: `--tap-console`, `--tap-profile`, `--tap-api-key`, `--tap-base-url`\n- Exit prints summary via `rp.Summary()` but NO resume command generation\n\n### logger package (`internal/logger/logger.go`)\n- `Init(dir string, consoleEnabled bool, level Level)` - consoleEnabled controls stderr output\n- Levels: DEBUG, INFO, WARN, ERROR\n- Console output only for INFO+ level (line 157: `if console && level >= INFO`)\n\n### config package (`internal/config/`)\n- `client.go`: `ClientConfig` struct, `ClaudeClient` var, `DetectTarget()`, `ResolveCmd()`, `BuildChildEnv()`\n- `claudeconfig.go`: Reads `~/.claude.json` for base_url. Has `HomeDir()` helper.\n- No profiles.json reading exists yet\n\n### proxy package (`internal/proxy/reverse.go`)\n- `NewReverseProxy(target, traceDir)` - currently only takes 2 params\n- `Summary()` returns api_calls, input_tokens, output_tokens, cache_read_tokens, cache_create_tokens\n- Has session ID extraction via `extractSessionID()` from request metadata\n\n### trace package (`internal/trace/writer.go`)\n- `DefaultTraceDir()` returns `$HOME/.claude-tap-plus/.traces`\n- `TraceWriter` with `Summary()` method\n\n## Three Features to Implement\n\n### Feature 1: Console Log Control\nPer the doc:\n| Flag | Log Level | Write File | Output to Console |\n|------|-----------|-----------|-------------------|\n| (none) | INFO | ✅ | ❌ | \n| `--tap-verbose` | DEBUG | ✅ | ❌ |\n| `--tap-console` | — | — | — | (alone, invalid) |\n| `--tap-verbose --tap-console` | DEBUG | ✅ | ✅ |\n| Backend mode (no flag) | DEBUG | ✅ | ✅ |\n\nCurrent code already handles `--tap-verbose` (line 163-167 of main.go). Need to add `--tap-console` flag parsing.\n\n### Feature 2: Multi-profile Configuration (profiles.json)\nNew file `~/.claude-tap-plus/profiles.json`:\n```json\n{\n  \"default\": \"anthropic-main\",\n  \"profiles\": {\n    \"anthropic-main\": { \"base_url\": \"...\", \"api_key\": \"...\", \"provider\": \"anthropic\" }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nNew CLI flags: `--tap-profile NAME`, `--tap-api-key KEY`, `--tap-base-url URL`\n\nPriority (high to low):\n1. `--tap-api-key` / `--tap-base-url` (CLI direct)\n2. `--tap-profile` (reads profiles.json)\n3. Environment variables (ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL)\n4. `~/.claude.json`\n5. Defaults\n\n### Feature 3: Exit Summary & Resume Command\nOn exit, print:\n```\n📋 Claude Code exited\n   API calls:      4\n   Input tokens:    1234\n   ...\n   Trace: ~/.claude-tap-plus/.traces/...\n\n📎 Resume:\n   claude-tap-plus --tap-verbose claude --resume <session_id>\n```\n\nResume mirrors original args + `--resume <session_id>`. Need to:\n1. Record `os.Args` at startup\n2. Strip existing `--resume <old-id>` if present\n3. Extract session_id (from proxy's trace writer or summary)\n4. Print resume command on exit\n\n## Design Constraints\n- Pure Go, no CGO\n- Follow existing patterns (logger.Debug/Info, etc.)\n- Backend mode keeps current behavior (DEBUG + console output)\n- Match Chinese comment style in existing code\n\nPlease provide a detailed, file-by-file implementation plan.","subagent_type":"Plan"},"tool_use_id":"call_3f49a292da8347a4b04ed3c8","tool_response":[{"type":"text","text":"This is critical. Line 157 shows the current constraint: console output only fires for INFO and above, even when `console=true`. For Feature 1, when `--tap-verbose --tap-console` is used, we need DEBUG-level logs to also go to stderr. This requires changing the logger to track the console minimum level separately, or removing the `level >= INFO` guard when verbose+console mode is active.\n\nNow I have all the information needed to design the plan. Let me write it.\n\n---\n\n## Implementation Plan: Three CLI Enhancements for claude-tap-plus\n\n### Overview\n\nThis plan covers three features to be implemented across approximately 6 files (4 modified, 2 new), with tests in 2 new test files. The changes are ordered by dependency: Feature 1 first (simplest, standalone), then Feature 2 (new config package file), then Feature 3 (depends on proxy having the session ID).\n\n---\n\n### Feature 1: Console Log Control (`--tap-console`)\n\n**Current state:** `main.go` line 163-167 shows that `--tap-verbose` sets `logger.Init(dir, true, logger.DEBUG)`. The second argument (`consoleEnabled=true`) is misleading -- when verbose, console is set to true, but the logger's `write()` function at line 157 has a hard-coded guard `if console && level >= INFO`, so DEBUG messages never reach stderr even in verbose mode. In non-verbose mode, console is false.\n\n**Required behavior:**\n- No flags: INFO level, file only, no console.\n- `--tap-verbose`: DEBUG level, file only, no console.\n- `--tap-console` alone: invalid (print error).\n- `--tap-verbose --tap-console`: DEBUG level, file + console (both).\n- Backend mode (no flag): DEBUG level, file + console (both, unchanged).\n\n#### Step 1.1: Modify `internal/logger/logger.go`\n\nAdd a new internal variable `consoleMinLevel` to track the minimum level for console output separately from `minLevel` (the file minimum level). Currently `console` is a bool; the change requires tracking a level threshold for console output specifically.\n\nChanges to the global variables section (around line 33-41):\n- Add `consoleMinLevel Level` variable.\n- When `consoleEnabled` is true and `level` is DEBUG, set `consoleMinLevel = DEBUG` (all levels go to console).\n- When `consoleEnabled` is true and `level` is INFO or above, keep `consoleMinLevel = INFO` (only INFO+ to console, current behavior).\n- When `consoleEnabled` is false, set `consoleMinLevel = ERROR + 1` (effectively disabled).\n\nIn `Init()`, after setting `minLevel` and `console`, add logic:\n```\nif consoleEnabled {\n    if level <= DEBUG {\n        consoleMinLevel = DEBUG  // verbose+console: all levels to console\n    } else {\n        consoleMinLevel = INFO   // default: INFO+ to console\n    }\n} else {\n    consoleMinLevel = ERROR + 1  // sentinel: no console output\n}\n```\n\nIn `write()`, replace line 157 `if console && level >= INFO` with:\n```\nif console && level >= consoleMinLevel {\n```\n\nThis is a backward-compatible change. When `backend_cmd.go` calls `logger.Init(logDir, true, logger.DEBUG)`, the new logic will set `consoleMinLevel = DEBUG`, so backend mode will output all DEBUG+ to console -- which matches the documented \"Backend mode: DEBUG + file + console\" behavior.\n\n#### Step 1.2: Modify `cmd/claude-tap/main.go` -- add flag parsing\n\nIn `runProxy()`, add a new flag variable alongside the existing ones (around line 110-115):\n```\ntapConsole bool   // 是否输出日志到终端（需配合 --tap-verbose）\n```\n\nIn the argument parsing loop (lines 118-155), add a new case:\n```\ncase arg == \"--tap-console\":\n    tapConsole = true\n```\n\nAfter the parsing loop, before logger initialization (around line 162), add validation:\n```\nif tapConsole && !tapVerbose {\n    fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"Error: --tap-console requires --tap-verbose\\n\")\n    os.Exit(1)\n}\n```\n\nModify the logger init block (lines 163-167):\n```\nif tapVerbose {\n    logger.Init(tapOutputDir, tapConsole, logger.DEBUG)\n} else {\n    logger.Init(tapOutputDir, false, logger.INFO)\n}\n```\n\nCurrently line 164 passes `true` for console when verbose -- this is wrong per the spec. The fix makes console conditional on `tapConsole`.\n\n#### Step 1.3: Update `printUsage()` in `main.go`\n\nAdd after the `--tap-verbose` line (around line 79):\n```\nfmt.Println(\"  --tap-console          Output logs to console (requires --tap-verbose)\")\n```\n\n---\n\n### Feature 2: Multi-profile Configuration (`profiles.json`)\n\n#### Step 2.1: Create new file `internal/config/profiles.go`\n\nThis file handles reading and resolving profiles from `~/.claude-tap-plus/profiles.json`.\n\n**Data structures:**\n```go\n// ProfileConfig 表示 profiles.json 中单个配置的定义。\ntype ProfileConfig struct {\n    BaseURL  string `json:\"base_url\"`           // 上游 API 地址\n    APIKey   string `json:\"api_key\"`             // API 密钥\n    Provider string `json:\"provider,omitempty\"`  // 供应商标识（anthropic/openai/gemini）\n}\n\n// ProfilesFile 表示 profiles.json 的完整结构。\ntype ProfilesFile struct {\n    Default  string                  `json:\"default\"`   // 默认配置名\n    Profiles map[string]ProfileConfig `json:\"profiles\"`  // 配置集合\n}\n```\n\n**Functions to implement:**\n\n1. `ReadProfiles() (*ProfilesFile, error)` -- reads `~/.claude-tap-plus/profiles.json`. Returns `nil, nil` if file does not exist (non-fatal). Uses `HomeDir()` from `claudeconfig.go` to build the path.\n\n2. `ResolveProfileConfig(profileName string) (*ProfileConfig, error)` -- if `profileName` is empty, reads the `default` field from profiles.json; otherwise looks up the named profile. Returns error if profile not found.\n\n3. `ConfigDir() string` -- returns `~/.claude-tap-plus/`, the base directory for all config. Reuses `HomeDir()`.\n\n**Path computation:**\n```\nfunc profilesPath() string {\n    return filepath.Join(ConfigDir(), \"profiles.json\")\n}\n```\n\n**ConfigDir function** should also be used by `trace.DefaultTraceDir()` in a future refactor, but for now just define it here.\n\n#### Step 2.2: Create new file `internal/config/resolve.go`\n\nThis file implements the priority resolution chain for API key and base URL.\n\n**Function signature:**\n```go\n// ResolvedConfig 包含解析后的最终配置。\ntype ResolvedConfig struct {\n    BaseURL  string  // 最终的上游 API 地址\n    APIKey   string  // 最终的 API Key（可能为空）\n}\n\n// ResolveTargetConfig 按优先级解析最终的上游配置。\n//\n// 优先级（从高到低）：\n//  1. cliBaseURL / cliAPIKey（命令行直接指定）\n//  2. profileName（读取 profiles.json）\n//  3. 环境变量（ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL）\n//  4. ~/.claude.json（Claude Code 配置文件）\n//  5. 默认值\nfunc ResolveTargetConfig(cliBaseURL, cliAPIKey, profileName string, cfg *ClientConfig) (*ResolvedConfig, error)\n```\n\n**Implementation logic** (pseudocode):\n```\nresult := &ResolvedConfig{}\n\n// Level 2: Profile\nif profileName != \"\" {\n    profiles, err := ReadProfiles()\n    if err == nil && profiles != nil {\n        if profileName == \"\" { profileName = profiles.Default }\n        if p, ok := profiles.Profiles[profileName]; ok {\n            result.BaseURL = p.BaseURL\n            result.APIKey = p.APIKey\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n// Level 1: CLI flags override profile\nif cliBaseURL != \"\" {\n    result.BaseURL = cliBaseURL\n}\nif cliAPIKey != \"\" {\n    result.APIKey = cliAPIKey\n}\n\n// Level 3: Environment variables (only if still empty)\nif result.BaseURL == \"\" {\n    if env := os.Getenv(cfg.BaseURLEnv); env != \"\" {\n        result.BaseURL = env\n    }\n}\nif result.APIKey == \"\" {\n    if env := os.Getenv(\"ANTHROPIC_API_KEY\"); env != \"\" {\n        result.APIKey = env\n    }\n}\n\n// Level 4: ~/.claude.json (only if still empty)\nif result.BaseURL == \"\" {\n    cc, err := ReadClaudeConfig()\n    if err == nil && cc != nil {\n        result.BaseURL = ClaudeBaseURLFromConfig(cc)\n    }\n}\n\n// Level 5: Default\nif result.BaseURL == \"\" {\n    result.BaseURL = cfg.DefaultTarget\n}\n\nreturn result, nil\n```\n\nNote: The priority for `--tap-base-url` overlaps with `--tap-target`. The requirement says `--tap-base-url` is equivalent to `--tap-target` but with higher priority. In the implementation, if both `--tap-target` and `--tap-base-url` are provided, `--tap-base-url` should win. The simplest approach: treat `--tap-base-url` as an alias for `--tap-target` that takes precedence, resolved in the flag parsing step.\n\n#### Step 2.3: Modify `cmd/claude-tap/main.go` -- add profile flag parsing\n\nAdd new flag variables in `runProxy()` (alongside existing ones):\n```\ntapProfile  string  // 配置名（读取 profiles.json）\ntapAPIKey   string  // 直接传入 API Key\ntapBaseURL  string  // 直接传入上游地址\n```\n\nAdd parsing cases in the argument loop:\n```\ncase arg == \"--tap-profile\" && i+1 < len(args):\n    i++\n    tapProfile = args[i]\ncase strings.HasPrefix(arg, \"--tap-profile=\"):\n    tapProfile = arg[len(\"--tap-profile=\"):]\ncase arg == \"--tap-api-key\" && i+1 < len(args):\n    i++\n    tapAPIKey = args[i]\ncase strings.HasPrefix(arg, \"--tap-api-key=\"):\n    tapAPIKey = arg[len(\"--tap-api-key=\"):]\ncase arg == \"--tap-base-url\" && i+1 < len(args):\n    i++\n    tapBaseURL = args[i]\ncase strings.HasPrefix(arg, \"--tap-base-url=\"):\n    tapBaseURL = arg[len(\"--tap-base-url=\"):]\n```\n\nAfter parsing, replace the current target detection logic (lines 170-177):\n```\n// 旧代码:\n// target := tapTarget\n// if target == \"\" {\n//     target = config.DetectTarget(&config.ClaudeClient)\n// }\n\n// 新代码:\nresolved, err := config.ResolveTargetConfig(\n    firstNonEmpty(tapBaseURL, tapTarget),\n    tapAPIKey,\n    tapProfile,\n    &config.ClaudeClient,\n)\nif err != nil {\n    log.Fatalf(\"resolve config: %v\", err)\n}\ntarget := resolved.BaseURL\n```\n\nAdd a helper function:\n```go\nfunc firstNonEmpty(ss ...string) string {\n    for _, s := range ss {\n        if s != \"\" { return s }\n    }\n    return \"\"\n}\n```\n\nWhen `resolved.APIKey` is non-empty, it needs to be injected into the child process environment. Modify the `BuildChildEnv` call or add the API key to the environment:\n```\nchildEnv := config.BuildChildEnv(&config.ClaudeClient, proxyURL)\nif resolved.APIKey != \"\" {\n    childEnv = append(childEnv, \"ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=\"+resolved.APIKey)\n}\n```\n\nUpdate `printUsage()` to add:\n```\nfmt.Println(\"  --tap-profile NAME     Use named profile from profiles.json\")\nfmt.Println(\"  --tap-api-key KEY      Override API key (highest priority)\")\nfmt.Println(\"  --tap-base-url URL     Override upstream API URL (highest priority)\")\n```\n\n---\n\n### Feature 3: Exit Summary & Resume Command\n\n#### Step 3.1: Modify `internal/proxy/reverse.go` -- expose session ID and trace path\n\nThe proxy already has `extractSessionID()` (line 356-375) and the writer tracks trace path. We need to expose the current session ID and trace file path to `main.go`.\n\nAdd two public methods to `ReverseProxy`:\n\n```go\n// SessionID 返回当前会话的 session_id。\n// 从追踪写入器的第一条记录中提取，如果尚无记录则返回空字符串。\nfunc (p *ReverseProxy) SessionID() string {\n    if w := p.getWriter(); w != nil {\n        return w.SessionID()\n    }\n    return \"\"\n}\n\n// TracePath 返回当前追踪文件的完整路径。\nfunc (p *ReverseProxy) TracePath() string {\n    if w := p.getWriter(); w != nil {\n        return w.Path()\n    }\n    return \"\"\n}\n```\n\n#### Step 3.2: Modify `internal/trace/writer.go` -- add session ID tracking and path accessor\n\nThe `TraceWriter` needs to:\n1. Track the file path (store it during `NewTraceWriter`).\n2. Track the session ID from the first record written.\n\nAdd fields to `TraceWriter`:\n```\npath      string  // 追踪文件路径\nsessionID string  // 从第一条记录提取的 session_id\n```\n\nIn `NewTraceWriter()`, store the `path` argument:\n```\nreturn &TraceWriter{\n    file:       f,\n    writer:     bufio.NewWriter(f),\n    modelsUsed: make(map[string]int),\n    path:       path,  // 新增：记录文件路径\n}, nil\n```\n\nIn `Write()`, after incrementing `w.count`, extract session ID from the first record:\n```\nif w.count == 1 {\n    // 从第一条记录提取 session_id\n    if sid, ok := record[\"session_id\"].(string); ok {\n        w.sessionID = sid\n    }\n}\n```\n\nAdd two public methods:\n```go\n// Path 返回追踪文件的完整路径。\nfunc (w *TraceWriter) Path() string {\n    return w.path\n}\n\n// SessionID 返回从追踪记录中提取的 session_id。\nfunc (w *TraceWriter) SessionID() string {\n    return w.sessionID\n}\n```\n\n#### Step 3.3: Modify `cmd/claude-tap/main.go` -- record args and generate resume command\n\nAt the start of `runProxy()`, record `os.Args` before any processing:\n```\noriginalArgs := os.Args[1:]  // 记录原始命令行参数，用于生成 resume 命令\n```\n\nIn the argument parsing loop, also track whether `--resume` was present and its value (to strip it later):\n```\nvar resumeID string  // 记录已有的 --resume ID，生成新命令时需移除\n// In the default case, before appending to claudeArgs:\ncase arg == \"--resume\" && i+1 < len(args):\n    i++\n    resumeID = args[i]  // 记录但不添加到 claudeArgs... \n    // Actually, --resume IS a claude arg, so it should still pass through.\n    // We just need to note it for building the resume command later.\n```\n\nWait -- `--resume` is a Claude Code argument, not a `--tap-*` flag. It passes through as a claude arg. For building the resume command, we need to strip `--resume <old-id>` from `originalArgs` and append `--resume <new-id>`.\n\nAfter the child process exits (around line 250), replace the current summary printing with enhanced output:\n\n```go\n// 打印运行摘要：API 调用次数和 token 使用情况\nsummary := rp.Summary()\ntracePath := rp.TracePath()\n\nfmt.Printf(\"\\n\")\nfmt.Printf(\"Claude Code exited\")\nif waitErr != nil {\n    fmt.Printf(\" with error: %v\", waitErr)\n}\nfmt.Printf(\"\\n\")\nfmt.Printf(\"   API calls:      %v\\n\", summary[\"api_calls\"])\nfmt.Printf(\"   Input tokens:    %v\\n\", summary[\"input_tokens\"])\nfmt.Printf(\"   Output tokens:   %v\\n\", summary[\"output_tokens\"])\nfmt.Printf(\"   Cache read:      %v\\n\", summary[\"cache_read_tokens\"])\nfmt.Printf(\"   Cache create:    %v\\n\", summary[\"cache_create_tokens\"])\nif tracePath != \"\" {\n    // 将绝对路径中的 HOME 替换为 ~，使输出更简洁\n    displayPath := shortenPath(tracePath)\n    fmt.Printf(\"   Trace: %s\\n\", displayPath)\n}\nfmt.Printf(\"\\n\")\n\n// 生成 Resume 命令\nsessionID := rp.SessionID()\nif sessionID != \"\" {\n    resumeCmd := buildResumeCommand(originalArgs, sessionID)\n    fmt.Printf(\"Resume:\\n\")\n    fmt.Printf(\"   %s\\n\", resumeCmd)\n}\n```\n\nAdd helper functions:\n\n```go\n// buildResumeCommand 根据原始命令行参数和新的 session_id 生成 resume 命令。\n//\n// 逻辑：\n//  1. 复制原始参数\n//  2. 移除已有的 --resume <old-id>（如果存在）\n//  3. 追加 --resume <new-session-id>\nfunc buildResumeCommand(originalArgs []string, sessionID string) string {\n    filtered := make([]string, 0, len(originalArgs))\n    skip := false\n    for i, arg := range originalArgs {\n        if skip {\n            skip = false\n            continue\n        }\n        if arg == \"--resume\" && i+1 < len(originalArgs) {\n            skip = true  // 跳过 --resume 及其值\n            continue\n        }\n        if strings.HasPrefix(arg, \"--resume=\") {\n            continue  // 跳过 --resume=id 形式\n        }\n        filtered = append(filtered, arg)\n    }\n    filtered = append(filtered, \"--resume\", sessionID)\n    return \"claude-tap-plus \" + formatArgs(filtered)\n}\n\n// shortenPath 将路径中的用户主目录替换为 ~。\nfunc shortenPath(path string) string {\n    home, err := os.UserHomeDir()\n    if err != nil {\n        return path\n    }\n    if strings.HasPrefix(path, home) {\n        return \"~\" + path[len(home):]\n    }\n    return path\n}\n```\n\n**Key design note on session ID extraction:** The `extractSessionID` in `reverse.go` extracts from request body metadata. However, the first API call may not have this metadata. An alternative approach: extract session ID from the `_internal/trace-init` endpoint, which receives it explicitly. We should store the session ID in `ReverseProxy` when `handleTraceInit` is called, and also in `TraceWriter` from the first record.\n\nFor the `ReverseProxy`, add a field:\n```\nsessionID string  // 当前会话 ID（由 trace-init 设置或从请求中提取）\n```\n\nIn `handleTraceInit` (line 410), after receiving `req.SessionID`, store it:\n```\np.sessionID = req.SessionID\n```\n\nThen `SessionID()` method returns `p.sessionID` first, falling back to the writer's session ID:\n```go\nfunc (p *ReverseProxy) SessionID() string {\n    if p.sessionID != \"\" {\n        return p.sessionID\n    }\n    if w := p.getWriter(); w != nil {\n        return w.SessionID()\n    }\n    return \"\"\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### Test Plan\n\n#### New test file: `tests/config/profiles_test.go`\n\nTests for the new `profiles.go`:\n1. `TestReadProfilesNotExist` -- profiles.json absent returns nil without error.\n2. `TestReadProfilesValid` -- reads a valid profiles.json fixture.\n3. `TestResolveProfileConfigDefault` -- resolves the default profile.\n4. `TestResolveProfileConfigNamed` -- resolves a named profile.\n5. `TestResolveProfileConfigNotFound` -- named profile not found returns error.\n\n#### New test file: `tests/config/resolve_test.go`\n\nTests for `ResolveTargetConfig` priority chain:\n1. `TestResolveCLIOverridesProfile` -- CLI flags beat profile.\n2. `TestResolveProfileOverridesEnv` -- profile beats env var.\n3. `TestResolveEnvOverridesClaudeJson` -- env var beats ~/.claude.json.\n4. `TestResolveDefaultFallback` -- falls back to default target.\n5. `TestResolveAPIKeyFromCLI` -- CLI API key takes precedence.\n6. `TestResolveAPIKeyFromProfile` -- profile provides API key.\n7. `TestResolveAPIKeyFromEnv` -- env var provides API key.\n\n#### Updated test: `tests/trace/writer_test.go`\n\nAdd tests:\n1. `TestTraceWriterPath` -- verifies `Path()` returns the constructor argument.\n2. `TestTraceWriterSessionID` -- verifies `SessionID()` extracted from first record.\n\n#### New test file: `tests/cmd/resume_test.go`\n\nTests for `buildResumeCommand`:\n1. `TestBuildResumeBasic` -- simple args get `--resume <id>` appended.\n2. `TestBuildResumeStripOldResume` -- existing `--resume <old-id>` is replaced.\n3. `TestBuildResumeStripOldResumeEquals` -- `--resume=old-id` form is stripped.\n4. `TestBuildResumeWithTapFlags` -- all `--tap-*` flags preserved.\n\n---\n\n### Implementation Sequence\n\n1. **Feature 1** (Console Log Control) -- no dependencies on other features.\n   - Modify `internal/logger/logger.go`\n   - Modify `cmd/claude-tap/main.go` (flag parsing and logger init only)\n   - Can be tested independently.\n\n2. **Feature 2** (Multi-profile) -- no dependencies on Feature 1 or 3.\n   - Create `internal/config/profiles.go`\n   - Create `internal/config/resolve.go`\n   - Modify `cmd/claude-tap/main.go` (new flags + target resolution)\n   - Modify `internal/config/client.go` (add `ConfigDir()` helper if shared)\n   - Tests: `profiles_test.go`, `resolve_test.go`\n\n3. **Feature 3** (Exit Summary & Resume) -- depends on proxy session ID being available.\n   - Modify `internal/trace/writer.go` (add path, sessionID fields and accessors)\n   - Modify `internal/proxy/reverse.go` (add SessionID, TracePath methods; store sessionID in handleTraceInit)\n   - Modify `cmd/claude-tap/main.go` (record args, build resume command, enhanced summary output)\n   - Tests: `resume_test.go`, update `writer_test.go`\n\n### Edge Cases and Risk Areas\n\n1. **Feature 1:** The logger currently passes `console=true` in verbose mode but the `level >= INFO` guard blocks DEBUG from console. The fix must ensure backward compatibility for backend mode, which calls `logger.Init(logDir, true, logger.DEBUG)` and expects all levels to console.\n\n2. **Feature 2:** `profiles.json` may not exist. The code must handle this gracefully (fall through to env vars / defaults). The `ConfigDir()` path `~/.claude-tap-plus/` already exists because `DefaultTraceDir()` creates `~/.claude-tap-plus/.traces/`. But `profiles.json` sits at `~/.claude-tap-plus/profiles.json`, not inside `.traces`.\n\n3. **Feature 2:** `--tap-base-url` and `--tap-target` overlap semantically. The design resolves this by merging them via `firstNonEmpty(tapBaseURL, tapTarget)`, giving `--tap-base-url` priority.\n\n4. **Feature 3:** Session ID may be empty if no API calls were made (user exits immediately). The resume command should only be printed when `sessionID != \"\"`.\n\n5. **Feature 3:** On Windows, `os.UserHomeDir()` may return different paths depending on the environment. The `shortenPath` function handles this, and `HomeDir()` in `claudeconfig.go` already has Windows-specific logic.\n\n6. **Feature 3:** The `--resume` flag and its value belong to Claude Code, not to `claude-tap-plus`. When passed on the command line, they pass through to `claudeArgs` via the default case in the parser. The resume command builder strips them from `originalArgs` to avoid duplication.\n\n### Critical Files for Implementation\n\n- `D:\\CodeDevelopment\\CodeProject\\claude-hk\\claude_tap_plus\\cmd\\claude-tap\\main.go` -- Central hub for all three features: flag parsing, logger init, target resolution, summary output, resume command generation.\n- `D:\\CodeDevelopment\\CodeProject\\claude-hk\\claude_tap_plus\\internal\\logger\\logger.go` -- Feature 1 core: must add `consoleMinLevel` variable and change the console output guard from `level >= INFO` to `level >= consoleMinLevel`.\n- `D:\\CodeDevelopment\\CodeProject\\claude-hk\\claude_tap_plus\\internal\\trace\\writer.go` -- Feature 3 foundation: add `path` and `sessionID` fields, `Path()` and `SessionID()` accessors, extract session ID from first record.\n- `D:\\CodeDevelopment\\CodeProject\\claude-hk\\claude_tap_plus\\internal\\proxy\\reverse.go` -- Feature 3: add `sessionID` field populated in `handleTraceInit`, add `SessionID()` and `TracePath()` public methods.\n- `D:\\CodeDevelopment\\CodeProject\\claude-hk\\claude_tap_plus\\internal\\config\\claudeconfig.go` -- Reference for `HomeDir()` pattern and JSON file reading; new `profiles.go` will follow this exact pattern."}]}]}
