point\n\n**Location:** `claude_tap_plus/internal/backend/api/health_handler.go`\n\n**Function Signature:**\n```go\nfunc Health(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {\n    logger.Debug(\"api.health\", \"health check\")\n    writeJSON(w, http.StatusOK, map[string]string{\"status\": \"ok\"})\n}\n```\n\n**Route Registration:** `claude_tap_plus/internal/backend/api/router.go`\n```go\n// Line 20: Health check endpoint\nmux.HandleFunc(\"/health\", Health)\n```\n\nThe health check is a simple HTTP GET endpoint that returns a JSON response `{\"status\": \"ok\"}` with a 200 status code.\n\n### 2. Proxy Mode Implementation\n\n**Location:** `claude_tap_plus/cmd/claude-tap/main.go` - `runProxy` function (lines 113-337)\n\n**Key Components:**\n\n**Child Process Management:**\n```go\n// Line 272: Start Claude Code as subprocess\ncmd := exec.Command(claudePath, finalArgs...)\ncmd.Env = childEnv\ncmd.Stdin = os.Stdin\ncmd.Stdout = os.Stdout\ncmd.Stderr = os.Stderr\n```\n\n**Lifecycle Management:**\n```go\n// Line 281-305: Signal handling and graceful shutdown\ngo func() {\n    sigCount := 0\n    for sig := range sigChan {\n        sigCount++\n        if sigCount == 1 {\n            // First signal: graceful shutdown to child process\n            fmt.Printf(\"\\n⏳ Shutting down Claude Code... (Ctrl+C again to force)\\n\")\n            _ = cmd.Process.Signal(sig)\n        } else {\n            // Second signal: force kill child process\n            _ = cmd.Process.Kill()\n        }\n    }\n}()\n```\n\n**Environment Variable Injection:**\n```go\n// Line 253: Build child environment with proxy URL\nchildEnv := config.BuildChildEnv(&config.ClaudeClient, proxyURL)\n```\n\n### 3. Backend Configuration Defaults\n\n**Location:** `claude_tap_plus/internal/backend/config.go`\n\n```go\nfunc DefaultConfig() Config {\n    cfg := Config{\n        Host:   \"127.0.0.1\",  // Localhost only\n        Port:   8080,         // Default port\n        DBPath: \"backend.db\", // SQLite file in current directory\n    }\n    logger.Debug(\"backend.config\", \"default config: host=%s port=%d db=%s\", cfg.Host, cfg.Port, cfg.DBPath)\n    return cfg\n}\n```\n\n### 4. Backend Server Startup\n\n**Location:** `claude_tap_plus/cmd/claude-tap/backend_cmd.go`\n\n**Key Process:**\n1. Parses command line arguments (port, db path, host)\n2. Initializes logger\n3. Creates server instance: `backend.NewServer(cfg)`\n4. Starts server with graceful shutdown\n\n**Server Implementation:** `claude_tap_plus/internal/backend/server.go`\n\n```go\nfunc (s *Server) Start() error {\n    // Cleanup timed out sessions\n    cleanupSvc := service.NewCleanupService(s.store.Sessions())\n    cleanupSvc.CleanupTimedOutSessions(context.Background())\n    \n    // Initialize services\n    issueSvc := service.NewIssueService(s.store.Issues())\n    sessionSvc := service.NewSessionService(s.store.Sessions())\n    \n    // Setup router with handlers\n    router := api.NewRouter(api.Handlers{\n        Issue:   api.NewIssueHandler(issueSvc),\n        Session: api.NewSessionHandler(sessionSvc),\n    })\n    \n    // Start HTTP server with graceful shutdown\n    srv := &http.Server{\n        Addr:    s.cfg.Addr(),\n        Handler: router,\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### 5. Backend Configuration for Skills\n\n**Configuration File:** `.claude/backend.conf` (referenced in test scripts)\n\n**Format:** Simple key-value file with `BACKEND_URL=http://127.0.0.1:19999`\n\n**Usage in Skills:**\n- Skills source `backend.sh` from `~/.claude/skills/backend.sh`\n- The `_load_backend_url` function reads `BACKEND_URL` from the config file\n- `_backend_available` function checks if backend is reachable (with 2-second timeout)\n- `_call_backend` function makes HTTP requests to backend endpoints\n\n### 6. Port/Service Availability Checking\n\n**Current Implementation:** No explicit port checking mechanism found\n\n**Existing HTTP Client Usage:**\n- Tests use direct `http.Get` calls for testing health endpoints\n- Shell scripts have `_backend_available` function that likely uses HTTP client\n- No built-in port checking in the proxy or backend code\n\n**Missing Infrastructure:** The project lacks:\n- Port availability checking before starting servers\n- Service health verification with retries\n- Port conflict detection mechanisms\n\n### 7. Key Patterns and Structures\n\n**HTTP Server Pattern:**\n```go\n// Common server structure in the project\nsrv := &http.Server{\n    Addr:    addr,\n    Handler: router,\n}\n```\n\n**Graceful Shutdown Pattern:**\n```go\nquit := make(chan os.Signal, 1)\nsignal.Notify(quit, syscall.SIGINT, syscall.SIGTERM)\ngo func() {\n    <-quit\n    srv.Shutdown(context.Background())\n}()\n```\n\n**Error Handling Pattern:**\n- All Go files use consistent error handling with `fmt.Errorf` and `%w` wrapping\n- Logging through the centralized logger package\n\n### 8. File Path Summary\n\n**Health Check:**\n- Handler: `claude_tap_plus/internal/backend/api/health_handler.go`\n- Router: `claude_tap_plus/internal/backend/api/router.go` (line 20)\n\n**Proxy Mode:**\n- Main: `claude_tap_plus/cmd/claude-tap/main.go` (runProxy function, lines 113-337)\n\n**Backend Configuration:**\n- Config: `claude_tap_plus/internal/backend/config.go`\n- Server: `claude_tap_plus/internal/backend/server.go`\n- CLI: `claude_tap_plus/cmd/claude-tap/backend_cmd.go`\n\n**Skills Integration:**\n- Config file: `.claude/backend.conf` (referenced in test scripts)\n- Shell utilities: Referenced in `~/.claude/skills/backend.sh`\n\nThis exploration reveals a well-structured project with clear separation of concerns, but lacks port conflict detection and health checking mechanisms that would be useful for robust service management."}]}]}
