[2026-05-30 19:16:17] [DEBUG] [PostToolBatch] os=windows python=/d/CodeDevelopment/CodeProject/claude-hk/.claude/localLanguage/python/python.exe
[2026-05-30 19:16:17] [INFO] [PostToolBatch] Input: {"session_id":"9bf82fe9-e376-4adb-95bb-300f36566835","transcript_path":"C:\\Users\\Administrator\\.claude\\projects\\D--CodeDevelopment-CodeProject-claude-hk\\9bf82fe9-e376-4adb-95bb-300f36566835.jsonl","cwd":"D:\\CodeDevelopment\\CodeProject\\claude-hk","permission_mode":"plan","effort":{"level":"xhigh"},"hook_event_name":"PostToolBatch","tool_calls":[{"tool_name":"Agent","tool_input":{"description":"Design backend auto-start plan","prompt":"Design an implementation plan for adding backend auto-start capability to the claude_tap_plus proxy mode.\n\n## Context\n\nThe project is at `D:\\CodeDevelopment\\CodeProject\\claude-hk\\claude_tap_plus/`. It's a Go project with:\n- `cmd/claude-tap/main.go` - entry point with `runProxy()` as default mode and `runBackend()` as a subcommand\n- `cmd/claude-tap/backend_cmd.go` - backend subcommand that parses flags and starts a backend server\n- `internal/backend/server.go` - `Server` struct with `NewServer(cfg)`, `Start()`, `Close()` methods\n- `internal/backend/config.go` - `Config{Host, Port, DBPath}` with `DefaultConfig()` returning `127.0.0.1:8080`\n- `internal/backend/api/health_handler.go` - GET `/health` returns `{\"status\":\"ok\"}`\n- `internal/backend/api/router.go` - registers `/health` route\n\n## Requirements\n\nWhen `runProxy()` starts (the default mode), it should:\n1. Check if the backend service is already running (by hitting the `/health` endpoint)\n2. If not running, automatically start the backend as a child process\n3. Manage the backend child process lifecycle alongside the proxy\n\n## Design Constraints\n\n- The proxy already starts Claude Code as a child process with signal forwarding\n- The backend defaults to `127.0.0.1:8080` with `backend.db`\n- The executable is `claude-tap-plus` (or `claude-tap-plus.exe` on Windows)\n- Must handle Windows (the dev environment is Windows)\n- Should reuse existing `backend.DefaultConfig()` and `backend.Config.Addr()` for the health check URL\n- Must clean up the backend process when the proxy exits\n- Should be simple - minimum code that solves the problem\n\n## Key Questions to Address\n\n1. Where exactly in `runProxy()` should the backend check/start happen? (before or after proxy setup?)\n2. How to get the current executable path to spawn `claude-tap-plus backend`?\n3. How to handle the backend child process lifecycle (start, wait, cleanup)?\n4. What timeout/retry logic for the health check after starting the backend?\n5. Should this be a separate function or inline in runProxy?\n\n## Existing Patterns\n\nThe project already uses:\n- `exec.Command` for child process management\n- Signal forwarding with `signal.Notify`\n- Logger for structured logging\n- `os.Executable()` is NOT used yet but would be the idiomatic way to get the current exe path\n\nPlease design a concrete implementation plan with specific code changes needed.","subagent_type":"Plan"},"tool_use_id":"call_b661a74e1cb54d4393204c37","tool_response":[{"type":"text","text":"I have all the information needed. Here is the complete implementation plan.\n\n---\n\n## Implementation Plan: Backend Auto-Start in Proxy Mode\n\n### 1. Problem Summary\n\nWhen `runProxy()` starts (the default mode), the backend service at `127.0.0.1:8080` may not be running. The proxy should detect this, auto-start the backend as a child process, and manage its lifecycle alongside the Claude Code child process.\n\n### 2. Architecture Overview\n\nThe implementation adds exactly **one new file** and makes **one small change** to an existing file. The core logic lives in a new file `cmd/claude-tap/backend_autostart.go` to keep `main.go` clean and the feature self-contained.\n\n```\ncmd/claude-tap/\n    main.go                 <-- modify: call ensureBackend() in runProxy()\n    backend_cmd.go          <-- unchanged\n    backend_autostart.go    <-- NEW: health check + spawn + lifecycle\n```\n\n### 3. Answered Design Questions\n\n**Q1: Where in runProxy() should the check/start happen?**\n\nAfter the proxy starts (line 236-244 of `main.go`) and before Claude Code is launched (line 272). The proxy must be running first because the `--settings` injection depends on the proxy URL. The backend check/start is independent of the proxy and Claude Code startup sequence, so it fits naturally between \"proxy is up\" and \"Claude is launched\". Concretely, it goes right after `log.Printf(\"proxy listening on %s\", proxyURL)` at line 244, before `config.ResolveCmd` at line 247.\n\n**Q2: How to get the current executable path?**\n\nUse `os.Executable()` -- already used in the project at `internal/session/meta.go:48` in the `BaseDir()` function. This returns the full path of the running binary (e.g., `D:\\...\\claude-tap-plus.exe`). Combined with `\"backend\"` as the subcommand argument, this spawns `<exe-path> backend`.\n\n**Q3: How to handle the backend child process lifecycle?**\n\nReturn a `*exec.Cmd` (or a small wrapper struct) from the start function. Use `defer cmd.Process.Kill()` in `runProxy()` to ensure cleanup. The backend process is independent of the Claude Code process -- it should be terminated when the proxy exits regardless of how Claude Code exits. Using `defer` in `runProxy()` handles all exit paths (normal, signal, fatal).\n\n**Q4: What timeout/retry logic for the health check?**\n\nAfter spawning the backend, poll `GET /health` in a loop with 200ms intervals, for a maximum of 5 seconds (25 attempts). If the backend does not become healthy within this window, log a warning and continue -- the proxy should not be blocked by a backend failure. The backend is a \"nice to have\", not a hard dependency for the proxy to function.\n\n**Q5: Separate function or inline?**\n\nSeparate function in a separate file. Three public functions:\n- `ensureBackend()` -- called from `runProxy()`, orchestrates check-then-start\n- Internal helpers for health check and process spawning\n\n### 4. Detailed Implementation\n\n#### 4.1 New File: `cmd/claude-tap/backend_autostart.go`\n\nThis file contains all backend auto-start logic.\n\n```go\npackage main\n\nimport (\n    \"fmt\"\n    \"net/http\"\n    \"os\"\n    \"os/exec\"\n    \"time\"\n\n    \"github.com/liaohch3/claude-tap/claude_tap_plus/internal/backend\"\n    \"github.com/liaohch3/claude-tap/claude_tap_plus/internal/logger\"\n)\n\n// backendHealthURL returns the full URL for the backend /health endpoint\n// using the default backend config.\nfunc backendHealthURL() string {\n    cfg := backend.DefaultConfig()\n    return fmt.Sprintf(\"http://%s/health\", cfg.Addr())\n}\n\n// isBackendRunning checks if the backend service is responding by hitting /health.\n// Returns true if a 200 response is received, false otherwise.\nfunc isBackendRunning() bool {\n    client := &http.Client{Timeout: 2 * time.Second}\n    resp, err := client.Get(backendHealthURL())\n    if err != nil {\n        return false\n    }\n    defer resp.Body.Close()\n    return resp.StatusCode == http.StatusOK\n}\n\n// startBackendProcess spawns the backend as a child process using the current executable.\n// Returns the *exec.Cmd so the caller can manage its lifecycle.\n// The backend runs with default config (127.0.0.1:8080, backend.db).\nfunc startBackendProcess() (*exec.Cmd, error) {\n    exePath, err := os.Executable()\n    if err != nil {\n        return nil, fmt.Errorf(\"get executable path: %w\", err)\n    }\n\n    cmd := exec.Command(exePath, \"backend\")\n    // Detach stdin/stdout/stderr so the backend doesn't interfere with\n    // the proxy's terminal I/O. Redirect to os.DevNull.\n    cmd.Stdin = nil\n    cmd.Stdout = os.DevNull // or a log file\n    cmd.Stderr = os.DevNull // or a log file\n    // On Windows, detach from parent console to avoid Ctrl+C propagation\n    // (the proxy handles its own signal forwarding).\n    cmd.SysProcAttr = nil // platform-specific: see note below\n\n    if err := cmd.Start(); err != nil {\n        return nil, fmt.Errorf(\"start backend: %w\", err)\n    }\n\n    logger.Info(\"autostart\", \"backend process started: pid=%d\", cmd.Process.Pid)\n    return cmd, nil\n}\n\n// waitForBackend polls the /health endpoint until the backend is ready\n// or the timeout expires. Returns true if healthy, false on timeout.\nfunc waitForBackend(timeout time.Duration) bool {\n    deadline := time.Now().Add(timeout)\n    client := &http.Client{Timeout: 500 * time.Millisecond}\n\n    for time.Now().Before(deadline) {\n        resp, err := client.Get(backendHealthURL())\n        if err == nil {\n            resp.Body.Close()\n            if resp.StatusCode == http.StatusOK {\n                return true\n            }\n        }\n        time.Sleep(200 * time.Millisecond)\n    }\n    return false\n}\n\n// ensureBackend checks if the backend is running, starts it if not,\n// and returns a cleanup function. The cleanup function should be deferred\n// by the caller to terminate the backend process on exit.\nfunc ensureBackend() func() {\n    // Step 1: Check if backend is already running\n    if isBackendRunning() {\n        logger.Info(\"autostart\", \"backend already running at %s\", backend.DefaultConfig().Addr())\n        return func() {} // no-op cleanup\n    }\n\n    // Step 2: Start backend as child process\n    cmd, err := startBackendProcess()\n    if err != nil {\n        logger.Warn(\"autostart\", \"failed to start backend: %v\", err)\n        return func() {} // no-op cleanup, proxy continues without backend\n    }\n\n    // Step 3: Wait for backend to become healthy\n    if waitForBackend(5 * time.Second) {\n        cfg := backend.DefaultConfig()\n        fmt.Printf(\"   Backend started at http://%s\\n\", cfg.Addr())\n        logger.Info(\"autostart\", \"backend ready at %s\", cfg.Addr())\n    } else {\n        logger.Warn(\"autostart\", \"backend did not become healthy within 5s\")\n    }\n\n    // Step 4: Return cleanup function\n    return func() {\n        if cmd != nil && cmd.Process != nil {\n            logger.Info(\"autostart\", \"stopping backend process (pid=%d)\", cmd.Process.Pid)\n            cmd.Process.Kill()\n            cmd.Wait() // reap the process to avoid zombie\n        }\n    }\n}\n```\n\nKey design decisions in this code:\n\n- **`isBackendRunning()`** uses a 2-second HTTP client timeout -- fast enough to not noticeably delay startup, slow enough to handle a slightly sluggish network stack.\n- **`startBackendProcess()`** uses `os.Executable()` which is already the project's pattern (see `internal/session/meta.go:48`).\n- **`waitForBackend()`** polls at 200ms intervals for up to 5 seconds. The backend typically starts in under 1 second on this project.\n- **`ensureBackend()`** returns a cleanup function rather than requiring the caller to manage the `*exec.Cmd` directly. This matches Go's `defer` pattern perfectly.\n- **Non-fatal behavior**: if the backend fails to start, the proxy continues. The backend is for issue tracking and session management -- the proxy works without it.\n- **stdout/stderr of backend**: redirected to `os.DevNull` so backend logs do not interleave with proxy terminal output. The backend already has its own file-based logger.\n\n#### 4.2 Windows Process Consideration\n\nOn Windows, child processes normally receive Ctrl+C signals from the parent console. Since the proxy already handles signal forwarding to the Claude Code process specifically, the backend child process should NOT also receive these signals. Two options:\n\n**Option A (Recommended - Simplest)**: Let the backend also receive the signal. The backend already handles SIGINT/SIGTERM gracefully in `server.go:59-66`. The proxy's `ensureBackend()` cleanup via `defer` will additionally call `cmd.Process.Kill()` which is safe even if the process already exited. This is the simplest approach and works correctly on Windows.\n\n**Option B (Windows-specific)**: Use `syscall.SysProcAttr` with `CREATE_NEW_PROCESS_GROUP` on Windows. This adds platform-specific code complexity for minimal gain since the backend already handles signals. Not recommended for the initial implementation.\n\n#### 4.3 Modification to `cmd/claude-tap/main.go`\n\nA single insertion in `runProxy()`, placed after the proxy starts (line 244) and before Claude Code resolution (line 247):\n\n```go\n    proxyURL := fmt.Sprintf(\"http://127.0.0.1:%d\", actualPort)\n    log.Printf(\"proxy listening on %s\", proxyURL)\n\n    // --- NEW: Auto-start backend if not running ---\n    cleanupBackend := ensureBackend()\n    defer cleanupBackend()\n    // --- END NEW ---\n\n    // Resolve Claude Code executable path\n    claudePath, err := config.ResolveCmd(&config.ClaudeClient)\n```\n\nThis is 3 lines added to `main.go`. The `defer cleanupBackend()` ensures the backend process is killed when `runProxy()` exits, regardless of the exit path (normal return, signal, `log.Fatalf`).\n\n#### 4.4 Cleanup Ordering\n\nGo `defer` statements execute in LIFO order. In `runProxy()` after the change, the defers will be:\n\n```\ndefer rp.Stop()            // registered at line 241 (existing)\ndefer cleanupBackend()     // registered after proxy start (new)\ndefer logger.Close()       // registered in main() at line 38 (existing)\n```\n\nExecution order on exit: `cleanupBackend()` -> `rp.Stop()` -> `logger.Close()`. This is correct -- the backend is stopped first (in case it needs the logger), then the proxy stops, then the logger closes.\n\n### 5. What NOT to Change\n\n- **`backend/config.go`**: No changes needed. `DefaultConfig()` and `Addr()` already provide exactly what we need.\n- **`backend/server.go`**: No changes. The server already handles graceful shutdown.\n- **`backend_cmd.go`**: No changes. The backend subcommand works as-is.\n- **`internal/backend/api/`**: No changes. The `/health` endpoint already exists.\n\n### 6. Testing Strategy\n\nA new test file `tests/backend/backend_autostart_test.go` can verify:\n\n1. **`TestIsBackendRunning_False`**: When no backend is listening, `isBackendRunning()` returns false. (Start a test HTTP server on a random port, call `isBackendRunning()` which checks 8080, verify false.)\n\n2. **`TestIsBackendRunning_True`**: Start a real backend server via `backend.NewServer(cfg)` + `srv.Start()`, then verify `isBackendRunning()` returns true.\n\n3. **`TestEnsureBackend_AlreadyRunning`**: Start a backend first, call `ensureBackend()`, verify it detects the existing backend and returns a no-op cleanup.\n\n4. **`TestEnsureBackend_StartsNew`**: With no backend running, call `ensureBackend()`, verify the backend becomes reachable, call the cleanup function, verify the backend stops.\n\nHowever, testing the actual subprocess spawning (`startBackendProcess`) requires the compiled binary to exist. These tests can be integration-level tests guarded by a build tag or a short-test flag.\n\n### 7. Edge Cases\n\n| Case | Behavior |\n|---|---|\n| Backend already running on 8080 | Detected by health check, no new process spawned |\n| Backend port 8080 occupied by different process | Health check returns non-200 or unexpected body -- treated as \"not running\", spawn attempt will fail with port bind error, logged as warning, proxy continues |\n| Backend fails to start (e.g., DB locked) | `startBackendProcess()` succeeds (process starts) but `waitForBackend()` times out, warning logged, proxy continues |\n| Proxy receives Ctrl+C | `defer cleanupBackend()` kills backend process after Claude Code exits |\n| Proxy crashes / log.Fatalf | `defer` still runs -- Go guarantees deferred calls on panic unwinding and normal returns, but NOT on `os.Exit`. Since `log.Fatalf` calls `os.Exit`, the backend process will be orphaned. This is acceptable -- the backend process will eventually be cleaned up by the OS or user. |\n\n### 8. Summary of Changes\n\n| File | Change | Lines |\n|---|---|---|\n| `cmd/claude-tap/backend_autostart.go` | **NEW FILE** | ~90 lines |\n| `cmd/claude-tap/main.go` | Insert 3 lines in `runProxy()` after line 244 | +3 lines |\n\nTotal: 1 new file, 1 file modified with 3 lines added. No changes to any other packages.\n\n### Critical Files for Implementation\n\n- `D:\\CodeDevelopment\\CodeProject\\claude-hk\\claude_tap_plus\\cmd\\claude-tap\\backend_autostart.go` -- new file, core auto-start logic (health check, process spawn, lifecycle management)\n- `D:\\CodeDevelopment\\CodeProject\\claude-hk\\claude_tap_plus\\cmd\\claude-tap\\main.go` -- single insertion point in `runProxy()` at line 244 to call `ensureBackend()`\n- `D:\\CodeDevelopment\\CodeProject\\claude-hk\\claude_tap_plus\\internal\\backend\\config.go` -- consumed by auto-start code via `DefaultConfig()` and `Addr()` (read-only dependency, no changes needed)\n- `D:\\CodeDevelopment\\CodeProject\\claude-hk\\claude_tap_plus\\internal\\session\\meta.go` -- reference for `os.Executable()` pattern already used in the project\n- `D:\\CodeDevelopment\\CodeProject\\claude-hk\\claude_tap_plus\\internal\\backend\\server.go` -- reference for understanding the backend server lifecycle and signal handling"}]}]}
