[2026-05-30 19:20:39] [INFO] [SubagentStop] Input: {"session_id":"9bf82fe9-e376-4adb-95bb-300f36566835","transcript_path":"C:\\Users\\Administrator\\.claude\\projects\\D--CodeDevelopment-CodeProject-claude-hk\\9bf82fe9-e376-4adb-95bb-300f36566835.jsonl","cwd":"D:\\CodeDevelopment\\CodeProject\\claude-hk","permission_mode":"plan","agent_id":"a59e426fc6149f074","agent_type":"Explore","hook_event_name":"SubagentStop","stop_hook_active":false,"agent_transcript_path":"C:\\Users\\Administrator\\.claude\\projects\\D--CodeDevelopment-CodeProject-claude-hk\\9bf82fe9-e376-4adb-95bb-300f36566835\\subagents\\agent-a59e426fc6149f074.jsonl","last_assistant_message":"Based on my exploration of the claude_tap_plus project, here's a comprehensive analysis of the session tracking and cleanup mechanisms:\n\n## **Session Tracking and Cleanup Analysis**\n\n### **1. Session Store Schema (SQLite)**\n\n**Sessions Table Structure:**\n```sql\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS sessions (\n    id               INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,\n    session_id       TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE,\n    machine_id       TEXT NOT NULL,\n    os               TEXT NOT NULL,\n    project_slug     TEXT NOT NULL,\n    project_cwd      TEXT NOT NULL,\n    transcript_path  TEXT NOT NULL,\n    local_trace_path TEXT,\n    model            TEXT,\n    source           TEXT,\n    status           TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'active',\n    registered_at    DATETIME NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,\n    closed_at        DATETIME,\n    close_reason     TEXT\n);\n```\n\n**Key Fields:**\n- `session_id`: Unique session identifier\n- `machine_id`: Machine identifier (format: username@hostname)\n- `project_slug`: Project identifier\n- `status`: 'active' (default) or 'closed'\n- `registered_at`: When session was registered\n- `closed_at`: When session was closed (NULL for active)\n- `close_reason`: Reason for closure\n\n### **2. Session Store Interface**\n\n**Function Signatures:**\n```go\n// RegisterSession registers a new session\nfunc (s *sqliteSessionStore) RegisterSession(ctx context.Context, sess Session) error\n\n// CloseSession closes a specific session\nfunc (s *sqliteSessionStore) CloseSession(ctx context.Context, sessionID string, reason string) error\n\n// ListSessions gets session list with filters\nfunc (s *sqliteSessionStore) ListSessions(ctx context.Context, filter SessionFilter) ([]Session, error)\n\n// GetSession gets single session details\nfunc (s *sqliteSessionStore) GetSession(ctx context.Context, sessionID string) (*Session, error)\n\n// CleanupTimedOut cleans up sessions registered over 24h ago that are still active\nfunc (s *sqliteSessionStore) CleanupTimedOut(ctx context.Context) (int, error)\n```\n\n**Session Structure:**\n```go\ntype Session struct {\n    SessionID      string     // Session unique ID\n    MachineID      string     // Machine identifier\n    OS             string     // Operating system\n    ProjectSlug    string     // Project identifier\n    ProjectCwd     string     // Project working directory\n    TranscriptPath string     // Transcript path\n    LocalTracePath string     // Local trace path\n    Model          string     // Model used\n    Source         string     // Source (startup/resume)\n    Status         string     // Status\n    RegisteredAt   time.Time  // Registration time\n    ClosedAt       *time.Time // Close time (nil if active)\n    CloseReason    string     // Close reason\n}\n```\n\n### **3. Session Service**\n\n**Function Signatures:**\n```go\n// SessionService handles session business logic\ntype SessionService struct {\n    store store.SessionStore\n}\n\n// NewSessionService creates a session service\nfunc NewSessionService(s store.SessionStore) *SessionService\n\n// Register registers a new session\nfunc (svc *SessionService) Register(ctx context.Context, sess store.Session) error\n\n// Close closes a session\nfunc (svc *SessionService) Close(ctx context.Context, sessionID string, reason string) error\n\n// List gets session list with filters\nfunc (svc *SessionService) List(ctx context.Context, filter store.SessionFilter) ([]store.Session, error)\n\n// Get gets single session details\nfunc (svc *SessionService) Get(ctx context.Context, sessionID string) (*store.Session, error)\n```\n\n### **4. Cleanup Service**\n\n**Function Signature:**\n```go\n// CleanupService handles timeout session cleanup\ntype CleanupService struct {\n    sessionStore store.SessionStore\n}\n\n// NewCleanupService creates a cleanup service\nfunc NewCleanupService(s store.SessionStore) *CleanupService\n\n// CleanupTimedOutSessions cleans up sessions registered over 24h ago\nfunc (svc *CleanupService) CleanupTimedOutSessions(ctx context.Context)\n```\n\n**Cleanup Logic:**\n- Cleans up sessions that are still 'active' after 24 hours\n- Sets status to 'closed' with reason 'timeout_cleanup'\n- Called once at server startup\n\n### **5. Session API Endpoints**\n\n**HTTP Routes:**\n```\nPOST   /api/session/register  - Register new session\nPOST   /api/session/close     - Close session\nGET    /api/sessions          - List sessions (with optional filters: machine_id, project_slug, status)\nGET    /api/session/{id}      - Get single session details\n```\n\n**Request Types:**\n```go\n// RegisterSessionRequest\ntype RegisterSessionRequest struct {\n    SessionID      string `json:\"session_id\"`      // Session UUID\n    MachineID      string `json:\"machine_id\"`      // Machine identifier\n    OS             string `json:\"os\"`              // OS type\n    ProjectSlug    string `json:\"project_slug\"`    // Project identifier\n    ProjectCwd     string `json:\"project_cwd\"`     // Project working directory\n    TranscriptPath string `json:\"transcript_path\"` // Transcript path\n    LocalTracePath string `json:\"local_trace_path\"` // Local trace path\n    Model          string `json:\"model\"`           // Model used\n    Source         string `json:\"source\"`          // Source (startup/resume)\n}\n\n// CloseSessionRequest\ntype CloseSessionRequest struct {\n    SessionID string `json:\"session_id\"` // Session ID to close\n    Reason    string `json:\"reason\"`     // Close reason\n}\n```\n\n**Response Types:**\n```go\n// SessionListResponse\ntype SessionListResponse struct {\n    Sessions []SessionListItem `json:\"sessions\"`\n}\n\n// SessionListItem (for list view)\ntype SessionListItem struct {\n    SessionID    string     `json:\"session_id\"`\n    MachineID    string     `json:\"machine_id\"`\n    ProjectSlug  string     `json:\"project_slug\"`\n    Status       string     `json:\"status\"`\n    RegisteredAt time.Time  `json:\"registered_at\"`\n    ClosedAt     *time.Time `json:\"closed_at,omitempty\"`\n}\n\n// SessionDetail (for single view)\ntype SessionDetail struct {\n    SessionID      string     `json:\"session_id\"`\n    MachineID      string     `json:\"machine_id\"`\n    OS             string     `json:\"os\"`\n    ProjectSlug    string     `json:\"project_slug\"`\n    ProjectCwd     string     `json:\"project_cwd\"`\n    TranscriptPath string     `json:\"transcript_path\"`\n    LocalTracePath string     `json:\"local_trace_path\"`\n    Model          string     `json:\"model\"`\n    Source         string     `json:\"source\"`\n    Status         string     `json:\"status\"`\n    RegisteredAt   time.Time  `json:\"registered_at\"`\n    ClosedAt       *time.Time `json:\"closed_at,omitempty\"`\n    CloseReason    string     `json:\"close_reason,omitempty\"`\n}\n```\n\n### **6. Answer to Your Question:**\n\n**Does the backend track active sessions and detect \"idle\" state?**\n\n**Yes, the backend DOES track active sessions** through:\n\n1. **Session Registration**: Each new session is registered with status='active'\n2. **Session Closure**: Sessions can be explicitly closed via API\n3. **Automatic Cleanup**: Timed-out sessions (>24h) are automatically marked as closed\n4. **Session Status Tracking**: The `status` field tracks whether a session is 'active' or 'closed'\n\n**However, there is NO mechanism for detecting \"idle\" (no active sessions) state** in the current implementation. The backend tracks individual sessions but doesn't provide:\n- A health check endpoint to see if there are any active sessions\n- A summary endpoint showing session statistics\n- A way to detect when all sessions are idle/closed\n\nThe cleanup service only runs once at startup and doesn't provide periodic cleanup or idle detection capabilities.","background_tasks":[],"session_crons":[]}
