[2026-05-30 19:29:29] [INFO] [SubagentStop] Input: {"session_id":"9bf82fe9-e376-4adb-95bb-300f36566835","transcript_path":"C:\\Users\\Administrator\\.claude\\projects\\D--CodeDevelopment-CodeProject-claude-hk\\9bf82fe9-e376-4adb-95bb-300f36566835.jsonl","cwd":"D:\\CodeDevelopment\\CodeProject\\claude-hk","permission_mode":"plan","agent_id":"a10aec38eea64be08","agent_type":"Explore","hook_event_name":"SubagentStop","stop_hook_active":false,"agent_transcript_path":"C:\\Users\\Administrator\\.claude\\projects\\D--CodeDevelopment-CodeProject-claude-hk\\9bf82fe9-e376-4adb-95bb-300f36566835\\subagents\\agent-a10aec38eea64be08.jsonl","last_assistant_message":"Based on my comprehensive research of the claude_tap_plus project, I can now provide a detailed report on the trace writing and session file mechanisms.\n\n## Complete Research Report: claude_tap_plus Trace Writing and Session File Mechanisms\n\n### 1. **Trace Writing Mechanism** (`claude_tap_plus/internal/trace/`)\n\n**File Structure:**\n- `anthropic.go` - Defines data structures for API trace records\n- `writer.go` - Core trace writing implementation\n\n**Key Components:**\n\n**TraceWriter** (`writer.go` lines 29-42):\n```go\ntype TraceWriter struct {\n    mu           sync.Mutex     // Concurrent write protection\n    file         *os.File       // Underlying trace file handle\n    writer       *bufio.Writer  // Buffered writer for performance\n    count        int            // Number of records written\n    inputTokens  int64          // Cumulative input tokens\n    outputTokens int64          // Cumulative output tokens\n    cacheRead    int64          // Cumulative cache read tokens\n    cacheCreate  int64          // Cumulative cache create tokens\n    modelsUsed   map[string]int // Model usage statistics\n    path         string         // Trace file path\n    sessionID    string         // Extracted from first record\n}\n```\n\n**WriteTrace Function** (TraceWriter.Write, lines 74-105):\n- **When called**: For every API request/response intercepted by the proxy\n- **File created**: Automatically creates directory structure and file if needed\n- **Session ID usage**: Extracts session_id from first record's request.metadata.user_id\n- **File check**: Does NOT check for existing files - appends to existing file\n\n**File Naming Convention** (lines 241-252):\n```go\n// Default fallback path: baseDir/{machineID}/{projectSlug}/{date}/{time}/pending.jsonl\nfunc NewTracePath(baseDir string) string {\n    machineID := MachineID()\n    project := DetectProjectName()\n    now := time.Now()\n    date := now.Format(\"2006-01-02\")\n    t := now.Format(\"150405\")\n    \n    path := filepath.Join(baseDir, machineID, project, date, t, \"pending.jsonl\")\n    return path\n}\n```\n\n**Final Session Trace Path** (lines 358-365):\n```go\n// With real session_id: baseDir/{machineID}/{projectSlug}/{date}/{time}/{sessionID}.jsonl\nfunc NewSessionTracePath(baseDir, machineID, projectSlug, sessionID string) string {\n    now := time.Now()\n    date := now.Format(\"2006-01-02\")\n    t := now.Format(\"150405\")\n    path := filepath.Join(baseDir, machineID, projectSlug, date, t, sessionID+\".jsonl\")\n    return path\n}\n```\n\n**DefaultTraceDir** (lines 202-210):\n```go\nfunc DefaultTraceDir() string {\n    home, err := os.UserHomeDir()\n    if err != nil {\n        return \".claude-tap-plus/.traces\"\n    }\n    dir := filepath.Join(home, \".claude-tap-plus\", \".traces\")\n    return dir\n}\n```\n\n### 2. **Proxy Session Tracking** (`claude_tap_plus/internal/proxy/reverse.go`)\n\n**ReverseProxy Structure** (lines 23-32):\n```go\ntype ReverseProxy struct {\n    target    string              // Upstream API target\n    baseDir   string              // Trace file base directory\n    writer    *trace.TraceWriter  // Current session trace writer\n    client    *http.Client        // HTTP client for forwarding\n    turn      atomic.Int64        // Request counter for turn numbering\n    server    *http.Server        // Local proxy HTTP server\n    startOnce sync.Once           // Ensure Start runs once\n    sessionID string              // Current session ID (set by trace-init)\n}\n```\n\n**\"Proxy File\" Reference**:\nThe \"proxy file\" refers to the trace file created by `TraceWriter.Path()`, which is:\n- Initially created as `pending.jsonl`\n- Renamed to `{sessionID}.jsonl` after `_internal/trace-init` call\n\n**Session ID Flow**:\n1. **Initial**: Empty string in ReverseProxy\n2. **Set via**: `_internal/trace-init` POST endpoint\n3. **Extracted from**: request.metadata.user_id (JSON format)\n4. **Used in**: `trace.NewSessionTracePath()` for final naming\n\n### 3. **Session Metadata Files** (SQLite Database)\n\n**Backend Session Storage** (`claude_tap_plus/internal/backend/store/session_store.go`):\n\n**Session Registration** (lines 21-71):\n```go\nfunc (s *sqliteSessionStore) RegisterSession(ctx context.Context, sess Session) error {\n    // Updates machines table (upsert)\n    // Updates projects table (upsert) \n    // Inserts session record with status = 'active'\n}\n```\n\n**Session Status Tracking**:\n- **Active**: Session is currently running\n- **Closed**: Session has ended (normal exit, timeout, error)\n- **Cleanup Service**: Automatically closes sessions >24 hours old\n\n**No JSON metadata files found** - uses SQLite database instead for session tracking.\n\n### 4. **Session Lifecycle in Proxy**\n\n**Complete Flow**:\n\n1. **Proxy Start** (`main.go`):\n   ```go\n   // Create reverse proxy instance\n   rp := proxy.NewReverseProxy(target, tapOutputDir)\n   actualPort, err := rp.Start(\"127.0.0.1\", port)\n   ```\n\n2. **SessionStart Hook** (called by Claude Code):\n   - Makes POST to `http://proxy:port/_internal/trace-init`\n   - Contains: session_id, machine_id, project_slug, transcript_path\n\n3. **Proxy trace-init Handler** (`reverse.go` lines 385-454):\n   ```go\n   func (p *ReverseProxy) handleTraceInit(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {\n       // Parse session info from request\n       // Create TraceWriter with session path\n       tracePath := trace.NewSessionTracePath(p.baseDir, machineID, projectSlug, req.SessionID)\n       writer, err := trace.NewTraceWriter(tracePath)\n       p.sessionID = req.SessionID\n       p.writer = writer\n   }\n   ```\n\n4. **API Request Interception** (`serveHTTP` lines 88-181):\n   - For each API request, create trace record\n   - Write to trace file via `p.writer.Write(record)`\n\n5. **SessionEnd Hook** (called by Claude Code):\n   - Makes POST to backend API to close session\n   - Updates status to 'closed' in database\n\n### 5. **Default Trace Directory Contents**\n\n**Path**: `$HOME/.claude-tap-plus/.traces`\n\n**Structure**:\n```\n{machineID}@{hostname}/\n  {projectSlug}/\n    {date}/\n      {time}/\n        pending.jsonl          # Initially, before trace-init\n        {sessionID}.jsonl      # After trace-init\n```\n\n### 6. **Session Metadata Files**\n\n**No standalone JSON files** found. Instead:\n\n1. **Backend SQLite Database**:\n   - Tables: `machines`, `projects`, `sessions`\n   - Tracks: session metadata, timestamps, status\n\n2. **Session Collection Metadata** (`claude_tap_plus/internal/session/meta.go`):\n   - File: `meta.json` in each session directory\n   - Contains: Session entries with file info, model usage, timestamps\n\n3. **Active Session Tracking**:\n   - Backend API for session listing/status\n   - Cleanup service for timeout management\n\n### Key Findings:\n\n1. **Trace files are JSONL format** - one record per API call\n2. **Session ID flows from hook to proxy to trace file naming**\n3. **No existing file checking** - trace writer appends to existing files\n4. **Uses SQLite database** for session metadata, not JSON files\n5. **Fallback naming**: \"pending.jsonl\" → \"{sessionID}.jsonl\"\n6. **Multi-level directory structure**: machine → project → date → time → session","background_tasks":[],"session_crons":[]}
