[2026-05-30 19:51:58] [INFO] [SubagentStop] Input: {"session_id":"9bf82fe9-e376-4adb-95bb-300f36566835","transcript_path":"C:\\Users\\Administrator\\.claude\\projects\\D--CodeDevelopment-CodeProject-claude-hk\\9bf82fe9-e376-4adb-95bb-300f36566835.jsonl","cwd":"D:\\CodeDevelopment\\CodeProject\\claude-hk\\claude_tap_plus","permission_mode":"acceptEdits","agent_id":"aabccda521ff97d10","agent_type":"Explore","hook_event_name":"SubagentStop","stop_hook_active":false,"agent_transcript_path":"C:\\Users\\Administrator\\.claude\\projects\\D--CodeDevelopment-CodeProject-claude-hk\\9bf82fe9-e376-4adb-95bb-300f36566835\\subagents\\agent-aabccda521ff97d10.jsonl","last_assistant_message":"Based on my exploration of the claude_tap_plus project, here's a comprehensive report on the session registration flow and file locations:\n\n## 1. **DefaultTraceDir and .claude-tap-plus path references**\n\n**File Path:** `internal/trace/writer.go` (lines 195-207)\n\n```go\n// DefaultTraceDir 返回默认的追踪文件存储目录，位于用户主目录下。\n//\n// 默认路径：$HOME/.claude-tap-plus/.traces\n// 如果无法获取用户主目录，则返回相对路径 \".claude-tap-plus/.traces\"\nfunc DefaultTraceDir() string {\n    home, err := os.UserHomeDir()\n    if err != nil {\n        return \".claude-tap-plus/.traces\"\n    }\n    dir := filepath.Join(home, \".claude-tap-plus\", \".traces\")\n    logger.Debug(\"trace\", \"default trace dir: %s\", dir)\n    return dir\n}\n```\n\n**Base Directory Structure:** `~/.claude-tap-plus/.traces/`\n- Contains machine ID directories (e.g., `Administrator@DESKTOP-12345`)\n- Under machine ID: project slug directories (e.g., `claude-hk`)\n- Under project slug: session trace files (e.g., `2026-05-30_150924_f9a252.jsonl`)\n\n## 2. **How `handleTraceInit` in `internal/proxy/reverse.go` creates trace files**\n\n**File Path:** `internal/proxy/reverse.go` (lines 392-454)\n\n**Function Signature:** `handleTraceInit(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request)`\n\n**Parameters received:**\n- `session_id`: Required from JSON request body\n- `machine_id`: Optional, defaults to `trace.MachineID()` if not provided\n- `project_slug`: Optional, extracted from `trace.ExtractProjectSlug(transcriptPath)` or `trace.DetectProjectName()`\n- `transcript_path`: Optional, used for project slug detection\n\n**Trace file creation flow:**\n1. Parse JSON request containing session info\n2. Extract/validate required `session_id`\n3. Determine `machine_id` (from request or automatically)\n4. Determine `project_slug` (from request, transcript path, or automatic detection)\n5. Call `trace.NewSessionTracePath(baseDir, machineID, projectSlug, req.SessionID)` to get path\n6. Create TraceWriter with `trace.NewTraceWriter(tracePath)`\n\n**NewSessionTracePath signature:** `NewSessionTracePath(baseDir, machineID, projectSlug, sessionID string)` (line 332)\n\n## 3. **Current `main.go` runProxy flow**\n\n**File Path:** `cmd/claude-tap/main.go` (lines 232-279)\n\n**Flow after proxy starts:**\n1. Line 233: Create reverse proxy instance\n2. Line 236: Start proxy listening\n3. Line 241: Set up defer to stop proxy on exit\n4. Line 243: Format proxy URL\n5. Line 244: Log proxy URL\n6. Line 247: Resolve Claude executable path\n7. Line 253: Build child environment variables\n8. Line 255-262: Inject authentication (API Key or Token)\n9. Line 265-269: Handle settings injection for Claude Code\n10. Line 272-276: Start Claude Code subprocess\n11. Line 285-299: Handle system signals for graceful shutdown\n\n**Backend.json checking would fit after proxy starts (line 244) and before resolving Claude path (line 247)**.\n\n## 4. **backend_cmd.go**\n\n**File Path:** `cmd/claude-tap/backend_cmd.go`\n\n**Backend start flow:**\n1. Line 22: Initialize with `backend.DefaultConfig()`\n2. Lines 25-50: Parse command line arguments to override config\n3. Line 52: Initialize logger using `trace.DefaultTraceDir()`\n4. Line 64: Create backend server with config\n5. Line 72: Start server\n\n**Backend config (lines 23-31):**\n```go\nfunc DefaultConfig() Config {\n    cfg := Config{\n        Host:   \"127.0.0.1\",\n        Port:   8080,\n        DBPath: \"backend.db\",\n    }\n    return cfg\n}\n```\n\n**No backend.json writing currently implemented** - the backend writes to SQLite database (`backend.db` by default).\n\n## 5. **Existing JSON file reading/writing utilities**\n\n**Found in these files:**\n- `internal/trace/writer.go`: Uses `json.Marshal` for writing trace records\n- `internal/proxy/reverse.go`: Uses `json.NewDecoder`, `json.Marshal`, `json.Unmarshal`\n- `internal/session/meta.go`: Likely contains JSON utilities for session metadata\n- Various test files show JSON reading patterns\n\n**Common patterns used:**\n```go\n// Writing JSON\njson.Marshal()\nos.WriteFile()\n\n// Reading JSON\njson.Unmarshal()\nos.ReadFile()\njson.NewDecoder(r.Body).Decode(&v)\n```\n\n## 6. **Project's trace base dir structure**\n\n**Actual directory structure found:**\n```\n~/.claude-tap-plus/\n└── .traces/\n    ├── [machine_id]/\n    │   └── [project_slug]/\n    │       └── [session_id].jsonl\n```\n\n**Example files:**\n- `~/.claude-tap-plus/.traces/claude-hk/2026-05-30_150924_f9a252.jsonl`\n\n**Directory path generation:** `DefaultTraceDir()` → returns `$HOME/.claude-tap-plus/.traces`\n\nThe trace files are JSON Lines format (JSONL), with each line representing an API call record. The structure follows machine → project → session hierarchy for organization.","background_tasks":[],"session_crons":[]}
